tion\nSuresh Kumar Mishra, M/s Aishwarya Group \nSuresh Parihar, M/s Mankind Pharma Ltd. \nSuresh. N,M/s Biocon Biologies Ltd.\nSurya Sahu, M/s MSD Pharmaceuticals Pvt. Ltd.\nSushil Kumar Sahu, CDL, Kasauli\nSushil Kumar Sharma, M/s Acme Generics\nDr. Swati Gupte, M/s DSM Nutritional Prod. India Pvt. Ltd. \nSwati Piramal, M/s Piramal Healthcare Ltd.: \nSweta Kotikalapudi, M/s Phenomenex India : \nSwetang K. Shah, M/s Zydus Cadila Healthcare\nDr. T. Narender, CSIR-CDRI, Lucknow \nTandraAdhikari, M/s Dusap Pharmaceuticals \nTanveer Shah, M/s Eris Lifesciences Ltd, \nTapan Sharma, M/s Rusoma Laboratories Pvt. Ltd.\nTarun Goel, M/s Procter & Gamble Health Ltd.\nTejeswari D, M/s Dr. Reddy’s Laboratories Ltd. \nThanga'Durai, M/s Geltec Pvt. Ltd.\nUday Kumar Singh, M/s Abbott India Ltd. \nUdhavKale, M/s Unichem L"},{"name":"INDIAN PHARMACOPOEIA COMMISSION","text":"IP 2022\nVinay Sharma, M/s Acme Generics \n; \n■\nVinayak Vele, M/s FDC India Ltd.\nViney Paul, M/s Sanofi India Ltd. \n-\nVinit Kumar Tiwari, M/s Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd/\nVinkalPanchani, M/s Sanofi-Synthelabo\nVinod Kumar Kansal, M/s Teva API India Ltd. \n<■ .\nViriod Nagarkar, M/s IP.CA Laboratories Ltd. \n..' .\nVishal Shukla, M/s Akums Drugs & Pharmaceuticals Ltd. :\nDr. Vivek Bansal, CDL,Kasauli \n„ \n■\nVivek Chanan, Soft Gelatin Capsules Mfg. ’s Association\nY. Madhu, NIB, Noida\nYogesh Shelar, CDSCO, New Delhi\nIn preparing the 9th edition of the Indian Pharmacopoeia i.e. \nIndian Pharmacopoeia 2022, the British Pharmacopoeia, the \nEuropean Pharmacopoeia, the United States Pharmacopoeia, \nthe National Formulary of India, the International \nPharmacopoeia, the Chinese Pharmacopoeia, the \nPharmacopoeia of Japan, the Pharmaceutical Codex, the Merck \nIndex and the standards published by the Bureau of Indian \nStandards have been taken into consideration. The Indian \nPharmacopoeia Commission expresses its thanks to the \nCommissions, Committees, Conventions and other \norganizations under whose authority these publications have \nbeen issued. At the same time, the Commission wishes to \nstate that if some errors have inadvertently crept into the \npresent compilation with regard to the statements of quantities \nor strengths or making quotations, such mistakes are in no \nway attributable to any of the publications mentioned above \nor to the authorities issuing them.\nWe acknowledge the contribution of the review of contents \nand comments on the final monographs by the group of \nexperts consisting of Shri J. L. Sipahimalani, ShriR. Sridharan \nand Shri R. Raghunandanan working with the technical \npersons and coordinating in the development of monographs.\nSpecialists from various organisations in India and \nabroad have rendered their support. These include the Central \nDrugs Laboratory, Kolkata; Central Drugs Testing Laboratory, \nChennai; Central Drugs Testing Laboratory Mumbai; Regional \nDrugs Testing Laboratory, Chandigarh; Central Research \nInstitute, Kasauli; Central Drugs Laboratory, Kasauli; All India \nInstitute of Medical Sciences, New Delhi; National Institute \nof Biologicals, Noida; Indian Veterinary Research Institute, \nIzatnagar; BARC, Mumbai; INMAS, Delhi; Food & Drugs \nLaboratory (I'DLj, Vadodara, Gujarat; Indian Immunological \nLtd., Hyderabad; WorldHealth Organization (WHO), Geneva;\nOrganisation of Pharmaceutical Producers of India (OPPI), \nMumbai; Vaibhav Analytical Services, Ahmedabad; Central \nInstitute of Medicinal & Aromatic Plants, Lucknow; Cipla Ltd., \nMumbai; Alembic Ltd,, Vadodara; Arbro Pharmaceutical Ltd., \nNew Delhi, Sun Pharmaceutical Ltd.; Natural Remedies\nCapsules Pvt. Ltd., Bangaluru; Torrent Research Centre, \nAhmedabad; Cadila Healthcare Ltd., Ahmedabad; \nNaprod Life Sciences Pvt. Ltd., Mumbai; Aurobindo Pharma, \nHyderabad; Glaxo Smith Kline Pharmaceuticals Ltd.; Sanofi \nIndia Ltd., Mumbai; Akums Drugs & Pharmaceuticals Ltd., \nHaridwar; Mankind Pharma, Gurugram, Abbott Healthcare, \nBaddi; Emcure Pharmaceuticals Ltd., Pune; RPG Life Sciences, \nMumbai; Mylan Pharmaceuticals, Hyderabad; 1PCA \nLaboratories Ltd., Mumbai; Serum Institute Ltd., Pune; Lupin \nPharmaceutical Ltd., Pune; Bharat Serum Ltd., Mumbai; Neon"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/administration-himachal-pradesh","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Administration, Himachal Pradesh"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Administration, Himachal Pradesh\nMember \t\nThe Joint Secretary (Regulation) \n(ex-officio) \nMinistry of Health & Family Welfare \nNirman Bhawan \nNew Delhi-110 011.\n(Dr. G. N. Singh)\nMember \t\nCommissioners in-charge of Drug Control \n(ex-officio) \t\nAdministration, Sikkim\nThe Scientific Body\nMember \t\nCommissioners in-charge of Drug Control \n(ex-officio) \t\nAdministration, Uttar Pradesh\n(Mr. Sudhir Kumar) \nJoint Secretary\nThe composition of the Scientific Body is given below:\nDr. (Prof.) N. K. Ganguly \nFormer Director General, ICMR \nC-191, 9th Floor\nMember \t\nThe Joint Secretary \n(ex-officio) \nDepartment of Pharmaceuticals \nMinistry of Chemicals and Fertilizers \n_Shastri Bhawan\nChairman\nDr. C. Adithan \nDirector-Professor, Dept. of Pharmacology \nJawaharlal Institute of Postgracigate Medical \nEducation and Research \nPondicherry-605 006.\nMember \n(ex-officio)\n, __\n...-... \n, \n4,9\nView Apartment \nof No. 199, Sector-35\nNew Delhi-110 011.\nida-201 301.\n-!'- --.--i._.,;_,__- ,,\nr•-• ,:)-`. \t\n......, \n„.._,\n$hri Sudhanshu Pant)\n--s,\nMember \t\nDr. Nitin Bhatia \nSr. General Manager (Tech. & Regulatory) \nIntas Animal Health \nIntas Pharmaceuticals Ltd. \n44th Floor, Premier House \nOpposite Gurudwara, S. G. Road, \nBodakdev, \nAhmedabad (Gujarat).\nMember \t\nProl(Dr.)Vmod Kumar Dixit \nFormer Dean, Faculty of Pharmacy & \nRetired Professor of Pharmacognosy \nDr. Hari Singh Gour University \n(formerly University of Sagar.) \nSagar, \nMadhya Pradesh.\nMember \t\nDr. Nitya Gogtay \nAssoc