at 271 nm.\nCategory. Oestrogen receptor antagonist.\nj with the mobile phase.\nDescription. Awhite or almost white powder.\nChromatographic system\nI - a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\n] octylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm) (Such as"},{"name":"Identification","text":"1 ChromSpher C8),\n| \n- mobile phase: a mixture of 70 volumes of solution\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with fulvestrant \nIPRS or with the reference spectrum of fulvestrant.\nStorage. Store protected from light.\nprepared by dissolving 0.2 g of potassium dihydrogen \nj phosphate and 0.25 g of cetrimide in 70 ml of water\ni adjusted to pH 7.0 with ammonia and 30 volumes of\nB. Enantiomeric purity (See Test).\nj propanol,\n| \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,"},{"name":"Tests","text":"Frusemide Tablets\nj - spectrophotometer set at 238 nm,\nAppearance of solution. A1.0 per cent w/v solution in ethanol\nj - injection volume: 100 pl.\nI"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/fumaric-acid","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Fumaric Acid"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Fumaric acid’\n0.2\nTenofovir impur\n■ •--! 0.43 - '\nity* 2-'• '■ \n\"\nTenofovir alafen \nabout .17 minuté\narri ide (Retention time :■’\n1.0\n'(^Fl-but-Z-ene.dioic acid, \n;> c:...n 't,- \n■ -n\n’({[1-(6-ainirio-9IApiirin-9-yl)propiin-2-yi]o.xy}mclhyl) ; phosphonic \nacid. 7. X Af'J? y \n¡ p/: ' : •\nInject reference solution (c).. The .test is not valid, unless, the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 3000 theoretical, plates, the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 for fumaric acid and tenofovir \npeak and the relative standard deviation for replicate injections \nis not more than 1.0 per cent for fumaric acid peak and not \nmorc tlian 5.0 per cent for tenofovir impurity peak.\nInj ect reference solution (c) and the test solution. a\nCalculate the content of fumaric acid and