;\n- spectrophotometer set at 260 nm, \n=;rfb/th r\n- injectionvolume: 10 pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n70\n■■''30AA<-.\nr..g -.b 12 \n-\n65 ....\n... ■\n•4. ^65'.'A:i :\n25\n■ 35\n35\n30\n' \n70v;\n40\n30\n42\n70\n30\nName-'' \nRelative Correction\n:?li \nretention time 'factor\nJ.D A - ; •! .A H A; D\" Di D \nA ' '' A-\n2i’~0xime'. . \n... . „\n0-52 .\nZ-Oximc2 .;. \nn .\n0.64 y ;\n9-Hydroxyrispcridone1 •<> ;\n0.71\n■ \n1.0\nDesfluoro risperidone4'5 F ;\n0.79\n- \n1.0 u\nRisperidone difluoroketone6\n6.90 '\n5-Huorori.speridone7 . \n,\n0?94; \n. :Z: JO\nRisperidone\n1.0\n1.0 : :\nRisperidone related compound G5 ,1,08.\n.. \n0.4 _\n6-Methylrisperidone5\nbl.44. ./ -\n•... 1.0 \n..\nIndividual unidentified impurities\n—\n. 1.0 .. A\nTotal impurities , , , . ; \n■\n—\na;'.,-//- \"tt•; ;a\n'3-(2-[4-[(E)-(2,4-Difluorophenyl)(hydroxyiinino)methyi]piperidin-l- \nylJcthyl)-2-methyl-6,7,8;9-tetrahydro-477-pyrido[l ,2-a]pyrimidin-4- \none,\n23-[2-[4-[(Z)-(2,4-Difluorophenyl)(hydroxyiniino)methyI]piperidin-l- \nyl] ethyl]-2-methyl-6,7,8,9-tetrahydro-4//-pyrido[l jS-aJpyrimichMl \none,\n2(9RS )-3-[2-[4-(6-Fluoro-i,2-benzisoxaz61-3“yi)piperidin-j-yl]ethyl]', \n9-hydroxy-2-methyl-6,7,8,9-tetrahyd^o-47y-py^iii6^1:,2-a]pyfiI^id^^,-\n4-One, \nA hA,; A-'\n43-{2-[4-(Benzisoxazol-3;-yl)piperidin-l-yl]ethyl}-2-methyl-6, hffi \ntetrahydrO'4j3-pyridd[i,'2'-d']pyfirnidin'-4-ohe; \" ''11'!jH\n5This impurity may hot be relevant to all manufacturing /processes,d\nIP 2022"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/ritodrine-hydrochloride-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Ritodrine Hydrochloride Injection"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Ritodrine Hydrochloride-Inj ection\nRitodrine Injection is a sterile solution of Ritodrine \nHydrochloride in Water for Injections.\nRitodrine Injection contains not less than 93.0 per cent and \nnot more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of ritodrine \nhydrochloride; C17H21NO3,HCI.\nUsual strength. 10 mg per ml.\nA. Dilute a suitable volume of the injection with methanol \n(30 per cent) to obtain a solution containing 0.01 per cent\nw/v of Ritodrine Hydrochloride. When examined in the range \n230 nm to 350 nm (2.4.7) exhibits a maximum at 275 nm and a \nshoulder at about280nm. \n?;\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the principal\npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Ritodrine Hydrochloride-Inj ection\nRitodrine Injection is a sterile solution of Ritodrine \nHydrochloride in Water for Injections.\nRitodrine Injection contains not less than 93.0 per cent and \nnot more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of ritodrine \nhydrochloride; C17H21NO3,HCI.\nUsual strength. 10 mg per ml.\nA. Dilute a suitable volume of the injection with methanol \n(30 per cent) to obtain a solution containing 0.01 per cent\nw/v of Ritodrine Hydrochloride. When examined in the range \n230 nm to 350 nm (2.4.7) exhibits a maximum at 275 nm and a \nshoulder at about280nm. \n?;\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the principal\npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution"},{"name":"Tests","text":"Related substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \n’\nTest solution. Dilute a volume of the injection, if necessary \nwith the mobile phase to obtain a solution containing 0.1 per \ncent w/v of Ritodrine Hydrochloride?\nReference solution (a). Dilute 1.0 ml of the test solution to \n50.0 ml with the mobile phase.\nReference solution (b). Heat a solution containing'0.1 per \ncent w/v ofritodrine. hydrochloride JPRSmthe mobile phase \ncontaining 5.6 per centv/wof sulphuric acid for 2 hours at \n85°. Cooland mix 10 volumes ofthe solution with 8 volumes of \na 10 per cent w/v solution of sodium 