m and 366 nm. Spray the\nDescription. A clear, pale yellow to amber yellow liquid, free \nfrom sediment and suspended matter, spicy, characteristic and\nsulphuric acid reagent and heat the \nplate at 105° for 10 minutes and examine in day light. \nThe chromatographic profile of the test solution is similar to\nanise-like odour."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Rosemary Oil\nReflux 2.0 g of powdered substance under \nxanunihion with 100 ml of n-hexane on water-bath for \n30 ipinutes, cool and filter. Concentrate under vacuum to 5 ml.\nPuskara\nRosemary Oil is the essential oil obtained by steam distillation \nof the twigs and blossoming tips of Rosmarinus officinalis\nPushkarmula, Orris root; Inula racemosa\nsolution. Reflux 2.0 g ofpuskara IPBRS with 100 ml \nof on water-b4t11 for 30 minutes, cool and filter.\nLinn. (Fam. Lamiaceae).\nRosemary Oil (Indian variety) contains not less than 2.0 per \ncent and not more than 10.0 per cent of borneol, and not less \nthan 15.0 per cent and not more than 40.0 per cent of a-pinene.\n£oncéhtratc under vacuum to 5 ml.\nApplÿ to the plate 10 pl of each solutionas band length 8 mm.\n^{owthbmobile phase to rise 8 cm. Dry the plate in air and \nexamine in thd ultraviolet light at 254 nm and 366 nm. Spray the\nDescription. A clear, pale yellow to amber yellow liquid, free \nfrom sediment and suspended matter, spicy, characteristic and\nsulphuric acid reagent and heat the \nplate at 105° for 10 minutes and examine in day light. \nThe chromatographic profile of the test solution is similar to\nanise-like odour."},{"name":"Identification","text":"that of the refercnce solution.\nA. \nDetermine by gas chromatography (2.4.13).\n■' A:7 \n'. \n. - \n..\nTest solution. A 2.0 per cent w/v solution of the oil under\nFofeigrt organic matter (2.6.1 ). Not more than 2.0 per cent.\nexamination in ethanolf95 per cent).\nEthanol-soluble extractive (2.6.2). Not less than 25.0 per cent.\nReference solution. A 2.0 per cent w/v solution of rosemary,\nWater-soluble extractive (2.6.3). Not less than 15.0percent.\noil IPRS mcethanol (95 per cent).\nPuskara consists of dried roots of Inula racemosa Hook. F. \n(Fam. Asteraceae).\nUs;e chromatographic, system described in the Assay.\nTotal ash (2.3.19): Not more than 5.0 per cent.\nAcid^in(ojubie ash (2.3.19). Not inore than 0.6 per cent.\nThe peaks, in the chromatogram obtained with the test solution\nPuskara contains not less than 0.05 per cent of alantolactone, \ncalculated on the dried basis.\ncorresponds to the peaks in the chromatogram obtained with\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). 1.0 g complies with the limit test for\nthe referencesolution.\nCategory. Anti-inflammatory,, antibacterial and aphrodisiac. 7; :\nheavymetals, Method B (20 ppm).\nB. \nFlash point (2.4.44). 118.0° to 122.0°.\nDescription. Brownish-grey externally, cylindrical root, \ncamphoraceous and taste is bitter. \n4: : .. \n; . ;\nLoss on (frying (2.4.19). Not more than9.0 per cent, determined\nTests W . .\non 5.0;g by drying in an oven at 105°.\nAssay Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14)"},{"name":"Identification","text":"A/w\nRelative density (2.4.29). 0.905 to 0.962.\nTest solution. Reflux about 2.0 g of the coarsely powdered\nsubstance under examination with 200 ml of methanol by \n.< ¿. =\n, \n.... \n,. \n. \n. \n„ . Refractive index (2.4.27). 1.458to 1.548.\nsoxhlet apparatus for 4 hours till extract turn colourless. Cool\nanti filter Concentrate under vacuum to 10 ml. \nOptical rotation (2.4.22). -6.0° to + 7.5°.\nA. Macroscopic — Root cylindrical, conical to fusiform in \nshape, unbranched, 5-12 cmlong and 0.5 to 2.0 cm in diameter; \nlongitudinally irregularly wrinkled and furrowed surface. Lateral \nrootlets very thin, wiry and brittle. Fracture, short and smooth.\nReferencesolution. A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of Acid value (2.3.23). Not more than 1.0 per cent.\nalanatolactone JPRS in methanol.. \nAssay. Determine by gas chromatography (2.4.13).\nB. Microscopic — Mature roots show a wavy outline due to \ndevelopment of rhytidoma, cork composed of 8 to 12 layejs \nthick walled, tangentially elongated, rectangular cells^ sefthe \nfilled with:reddish-brown contents) Cambium is not distinct; \nparenchyma in general contains granular, slightly yellowish \nor colourless inulin granules and also a few yellowish.oil \nglobules; starch grains either absent or very rarely seenin \ncortical and ray cells; yellowish resinous masscs present fo \nsecretary'canals. \n(¿.A w\nChromatographic system . \n; \nTest solution. A 2.0 per cent w/v solution of the oil under\n- a stainless steel column 30 cm x 4.6 mm packed with\nexamination in ethanol (95 per cent).\nOctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (10 pm),\nReference solution (a). A 2.0 per cent w/v solution of borneol\n, \nmobile phase: a mixture of 70 volumes of aceionitrile\nIPRS in ethanol (95 per cent).\nand 30 volumes of water, \nflow fate: 1 ml per minute,\nReference solution (b). A 2.0 per cent w/v solution Of a-pinëne\nIPRS methanol (95 per cent).\nspectrophotometer set as 210 nm, \ninjection volume: 20 pl.\nPowder is reddish-brown; shows abundant prismatic crystal? \nof inulin s Cattere d th rough o u t p af e n chy matous cells)); \nfragments of polygonal to rectangular cells. Parenchymatous \ncells of phellpderm;are filled with the broym contents. ? i\nChromatographic system\n- a capillary column 30 m x 0.25 mm, coated with methyl\nInject the reference solution. The relative standard deviation\n5 per cent phenylpolysiloxane,\ntemperature: \n. \n_ .\ncolumn. 50° for 1 minute, increase from.50° to 220° ata\nfor the replicate injection is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nfoject the reference solution and the test solution.- . .\n■........: \n■ NN3 w., \n< --wyw \n.■ :\nC. Determine by thin layer chromatography (2.4.17) coating \nthe plate with silica gel GF254.. ).'■ y.; y ... \n/'/Sy '■\n, for 13 minutes, , \n? c\n- inlet port at 250° and detector at 280°,\n.. rate of 10° per minute and .maintain at this temperature\nCalculate the content of alantolactone.\nSforage. Store protected from heat, moisture and against attack\nMobile phase A mixture of 93 volumes of toluene^ \n7 volumes of' ethyl acetate, \n• ...... J \n' •’\ninsects and rodents.\n4282\n-Ta\nI®\n4283"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosiglitazone-maleate-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosiglitazone Maleate Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Rosiglitazone Maleate Tablets\nRosiglitazone Tablets contains not less than 90.0 per cent and\nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of\nrosiglitazone, ClsH19N303S,\nUsual strengths. 1mg; 2 mg; 4 mg."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Rosiglitazone Maleate Tablets\nRosiglitazone Tablets contains not less than 90.0 per cent and\nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of\nrosiglitazone, ClsH19N303S,\nUsual strengths. 1mg; 2 mg; 4 mg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained\nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the\nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Dissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No.1,\nMedium. 900 ml of0.1 M hydrochloric acid,\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm for 30 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume ofthe medium and filter promptly\nthrough a membrane filter disc having an average pore diameter\nnot greater than 1.0 J.!m, rejecting the first 1 ml ofthe filtrate.\nDilute the filtrate, ifnecessary, with the same solvent. Measure\nthe absorbance of the resulting solution at the maximum at\nabout 318 urn (2.4.7). Similarly measure the absorbance of a\nstandard solution of known concentration of rosiglitazone\nmaleate RS and calculate the content ofClsH,9N303S.\nD. Not less than 70 per cent of the stated amount of\nClsH19N303S.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Weigh accurately a quantity ofpowdered tablets\ncontaining 200 mg of Rosiglitazone, disperse in 100.0 ml of\nmobile phase. Centrifuge and use clear supernatant liquid.\nReference solution (a). A 0.2 per cent w/v solution of\nrosiglitazone maleate RS in the mobile phase.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1ml ofreference solution (a) to\n100 ml with mobile phase.\nUse the chromatographic system described under Assay.\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the\ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the column efficiency in\nnot less than 2000 theoretical plates.\nInject the test solution and reference solution (b). In the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area ofany\nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the peak in the\nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (1.0 per\ncent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks is not\nmore than twice the area of the peak in the chromatogram\nobtained with the reference solution (b) (2.0 per cent). Ignore\nany peak (due to maleic acid) with a relative retention time of\nabout 0.4.\nUniformity of content. Comply with the tests stated under\nTablets.\nDisperse 1 tablet in 0.1 M hydrochloric acid to produce\n0.004 per cent w/v solution. Measure the absorbance of the\nresulting solution at the maximum at about 318 nm (2.4.7).\nCalculate the content of CIsHI9N303S from the absorbance\nobtained from same concentration of rosiglitazone maleate\nRS in the same medium.\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Weigh accurately\na quantity of powdered tablets containing 20 mg of\nRosiglitaZone, disperse in 100.0ml ofmobile phase. Centrifuge\nand use clear supernatant liquid.\nReference solution. A 0.020 per cent w/v solution of\nrosiglitaione maleate RS in mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\n-\na stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm packed with\noctadecysilane bonded to porous silica (5 11m),"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosiglitazone-maleate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosiglitazone Maleate"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"ROSIGLITAZONE MALEATE\nRosiglitazone Maleate\n(COOH\nCOOH\nClsHI9N303S,CJ1404\nMol. Wt. 473.5\nRosiglitazone Maleate is (RS)-5-{p-[2-(methyl-2-pyridylamino)\nethoxy]benzyl}-2,4-thiazolidinedione maleate (1: 1).\nRosiglitazone Maleate contains not less than 98.0 per cent\nand not more than 102.0 per cent of ClsHI9N303S,C4H404,\ncalculated on the anhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antidibatic\nDescription. A white to off-white crystalline powder."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"ROSIGLITAZONE MALEATE\nRosiglitazone Maleate\n(COOH\nCOOH\nClsHI9N303S,CJ1404\nMol. Wt. 473.5\nRosiglitazone Maleate is (RS)-5-{p-[2-(methyl-2-pyridylamino)\nethoxy]benzyl}-2,4-thiazolidinedione maleate (1: 1).\nRosiglitazone Maleate contains not less than 98.0 per cent\nand not more than 102.0 per cent of ClsHI9N303S,C4H404,\ncalculated on the anhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antidibatic\nDescription. A white to off-white crystalline powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6).\nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with rosiglitazone\nmaleate RS."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Related substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 25 mg of the substance under\nexamination in 50 ml ofmobile phase.\nReference solution (a). A 0.05 per cent w/v solution of\nrosiglitazone maleate RS in the mobile phase.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1ml ofreference solution (a) to\n100 ml with mobile phase.\nUse the chromatographic system described under Assay.\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the\ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the column efficiency in\nnot less than 2000 theoretical plates.\nInject the test solution and reference solution (b). In the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area ofany\nsecondary peak is not more than 0.5 times the area ofthe peak\nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (b)\n(0.5 per cent) and the sum ofareas ofall the secondary peaks\nis not more than the area of the peak in the chromatogram\nobtained with the reference solution (b) (1.0 per cent). Ignore\nany peak (due to maleic acid) with a relative retention time of\nabout 0.4.\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). Lgcomplies withthe limittestfor heavy\nmetals, Metboc1BJ20ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Notmore than 0.5 percent, determined on 1.0 g.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Dissolve 20 mg of the substance under\nexamination in 100.0 ml ofmobile phase.\nReference solution. A\n0.020 per cent w/v solution of\nrosiglitazone maleate RS in mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\n-\na stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 J.!m),\n-\nmobile phase: a mixture of65 volumes ofbuffersolution\nprepared by dissolving 1.36 g ofpotassium dihydrogen\northophosphate in 1000 ml ofwater and adjust the pH\nto 3.0 with dilute phosphoric acid, 25 volumes of\nacetonitrile and 10 volumes of methanol,\nflow rate. 1ml perminute,\nspectrophotometer set at 235 nm,\n-\ninjection volume. 10 J.!l.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the\nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections is not more\nthan 2.0 per cent.\nInject the test solution and the reference solution.\nCalculate the content ofClsHI9N303S,C4H404.\nStorage. Store protected from light.\nRosiglitazone Tablets"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosiglitazone-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosiglitazone Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"RosiglitazoneTablets\nRosuvastatinCalcium\nRosuvastatinTablets\nRoxithromycin\nRoxithromycinTablets\nRabeprazole Sodium\nMol. Wt. 381.4\nRabeprazole sodium is 2-({[4-(3-methoxypropoxy)-3-methyl-\n2-pyridinyl]methyl}sulphinyl)-IH-benzimidazole sodium.\nRabeprazole sodium contains not less than 98.0 per cent and\nnot more than 102.0 per cent ofClsHzoN303S,Na, calculated on\nthe anhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antiulcer.\nDescription. A white to light yellow, crystalline powder,\nhygroscopic."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"RosiglitazoneTablets\nRosuvastatinCalcium\nRosuvastatinTablets\nRoxithromycin\nRoxithromycinTablets\nRabeprazole Sodium\nMol. Wt. 381.4\nRabeprazole sodium is 2-({[4-(3-methoxypropoxy)-3-methyl-\n2-pyridinyl]methyl}sulphinyl)-IH-benzimidazole sodium.\nRabeprazole sodium contains not less than 98.0 per cent and\nnot more than 102.0 per cent ofClsHzoN303S,Na, calculated on\nthe anhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antiulcer.\nDescription. A white to light yellow, crystalline powder,\nhygroscopic."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6).\nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with rabeprazole\nsodium RS.\nB. A 10 per cent w/v solution in carbon dioxide-free water\ngives reaction ofsodium (2.3.1)."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Related substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 80 volumes ofmethanol, 20 volumes ofwater\nand 0.1 volume ofdiethylamine.\nTest solution. Dissolve 50 mg of the substance under\nexamination in 100 ml with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (a). A 0.05 per cent w/v solution of\nrabeprazole sodium RS in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1 ml ofreference solution (a) to\n100 ml with solventmixture.\nChromatographic system as described under Assay.\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the\ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the column efficiency in\nnot less than 2000 theoretical plates.\nInject the test solution and reference solution (b). Run the\nchromatogram three times of the principal peale In the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area ofany\nsecondary peak is not more than 0.5 times the area ofthe peak\nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (b)\n(0.5 per cent) and the sum ofareas ofall the secondary peaks\nis not more than 1.5 times the area ofthe peak in the chroma-\ntogram obtained with the reference solution (b) (1.5 per cent)."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosuvastatin-and-ezetimibe-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosuvastatin and Ezetimibe Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"0,2018\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1 ml of reference solution (a) t o\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\n 10 ml with mobile phase.\nCalculate the content of C 22H28FN306S.\nChromatographic system as described under Assay.\nUse chromatographic system, solvent mixture and test \nsolution as described under Assay.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nInject reference solution (a). The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates and \nthe tailing factor is not more than 2.0.\nLabelling. The label states the strength in terms of the \nequivalent amount of Rosuvastatin.\nInject the test solution. The area of any secondary peak is \nnot more than 1.0 per cent and the sum of areas of all the \nsecondary peaks is not more than 2.0 per cent, calculated by \narea normalisation.\nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than 1.5 times the area of the peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) \n(1.5 per cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks \nis not more than 3.0 times the area of the peak in the chromato-\ngram obtained with reference solution (b) (3.0 per cent)."},"sections":[{"name":"ROSUVASTATIN AND EZETIMIBE TABLETS","text":"0,2018\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1 ml of reference solution (a) t o\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\n 10 ml with mobile phase.\nCalculate the content of C 22H28FN306S.\nChromatographic system as described under Assay.\nUse chromatographic system, solvent mixture and test \nsolution as described under Assay.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nInject reference solution (a). The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates and \nthe tailing factor is not more than 2.0.\nLabelling. The label states the strength in terms of the \nequivalent amount of Rosuvastatin.\nInject the test solution. The area of any secondary peak is \nnot more than 1.0 per cent and the sum of areas of all the \nsecondary peaks is not more than 2.0 per cent, calculated by \narea normalisation.\nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than 1.5 times the area of the peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) \n(1.5 per cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks \nis not more than 3.0 times the area of the peak in the chromato-\ngram obtained with reference solution (b) (3.0 per cent)."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosuvastatin-calcium-and-ezetimibe-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Ezetimibe Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Ezetimibe Tablets : \nJ\nRosuvastatin and Ezetimibe Tablets contain not less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated \namount of rosuvastatin, C^H28FN3O6S and,ezetimibe\nc^h21f2no3. \n, v. \n’I\nUsual strengths. Rosuvastatin 5 mg, Ezetimibe 10 mg; 7 \nRosuvastatin 20 mg, Ezetimibe 10 mg; Rosuvastatin 40 mg, 4 \nEzetimibe 10mg. , \n.......... 7"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Ezetimibe Tablets : \nJ\nRosuvastatin and Ezetimibe Tablets contain not less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated \namount of rosuvastatin, C^H28FN3O6S and,ezetimibe\nc^h21f2no3. \n, v. \n’I\nUsual strengths. Rosuvastatin 5 mg, Ezetimibe 10 mg; 7 \nRosuvastatin 20 mg, Ezetimibe 10 mg; Rosuvastatin 40 mg, 4 \nEzetimibe 10mg. , \n.......... 7"},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the principal peaks in the.chromatogram obtained I \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peaks in the i \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution', . ....\nTests'' f .,.. \n. . \n1\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No?2 (Paddle), \n■ \n•'\nMedium, 90Q.ml of a buffer solution.prepared by dissolving 10 \ng of sodium lauryl sulphate in 1000 ml of water, \nSpeed and time. 50 rpmfor 45 .minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter, rejecting\n, the first few ml of the filtrate.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). ,\nTest solution. The filtrate obtained as given above, diluted \nsuitably if necessary, with the dissolution medium,\nReference solution. Dissolve an accurately weighed quantity\nof rosuvastatin calcium IPRS arid ezetimibe IPRS in the \nsolvent mixture and dilute with the dissolution medium to \nobtain á solution having a known concentration similar to the \nexpected concentration of the test' solution. ' ' ' 7\nUse chromatographic system (except the requirement of sample \ntemperature 5 °) and solvent mixture as described under Assay-\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. TE'ET\nCalculate the contents of C22H28FN3O6S arid \n.\nthe tablets. \nJ : '\nQ. Not less than 70 per cent of the stated ahiourits of\nC22H2SFN3O6SandjC24H2!F2NO3.\ntp2022\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography\n(2.4.14). \n......\nc¡iromatographic system, solvent mixture and test \n^tóiMtócrí^dXinderAssa^\ní ct the test solution. The area of any secondary peak is not \njnorethan l.Opct cent and the sum of areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 2.0 per cent, calculated by area\nnormalisation.\nUniformity of content. Complies with the test stated under\nTablets.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Disperse one tablet with 70 ml of solvent mixture \nultrasound for 10 minutes, add sufficient solvent mixture to \nproduce 100.0 ml, mix, centrifuge at 2500 rpm for about 20 \nminutes and filter. Dilute the filtrate, if necessary.\nUse chromatographic system, solvent mixture and reference \nsolution described under Assay. .\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the contents of C22H28FN;;()6S and C2.;H2I'2NCL in\nthei tablets. .\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay; Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14)."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Solvent mixture. 50 volumes of dimethyl formamide and 50 \nvolumes of methanol.\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof the powdercontaining about 5. mg of Rosuvastatin. with 70 \nml of solvent mixture, ultrasound for 10 minutes, add sufficient \nsolvent mixture to produce 100.0 ml, mix and filter."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Reference solution. A solution containing 0.053 per cent w/v \nof rosuvastatin calcium IP RS and 0,1 per cent w/v solution of \neeetimihe IPRS in solvent mixture. Dilute to 1.0 ml to 10.0 \nml with solvent mixture to obtain a solution having a known \nconcentration similar to the test solution.\nChromatographic system\na stainless- steel column 25 cm ' 4.6- mm, packed \nwith dctadecy tsi lane chemically bonded to porous silica \n(5|mi)(Such as Hypersil BDS), =\n- sampietemperaiure: 5°,\n- mobile phase: a;.mixture of 600 volumes of a buffer\nsolution prepared by dissolving 0.77 g of ammonium \nacetate > ini 1000 ml of water, 400 volumes of \nacetonitrile and> 5 volumes of triethylamine mix \narid adjusted to pH 4.0 with dilute orthophosphoric\n; acid,\n~ how rate: 1.5 ml per minute,\n' spectrophotometer set al 230 nm, \n'injection volume: 20 pl."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosuvastatin-calcium-and-fenofibrate-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Fenofibrate Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Fenofibrate Tablets\nRosuvastatin. and Fenofibrate Tablets contain not less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated \namount of rosuvastatin, C22H28FN3O6S and fenofibrate, \nC20H2IClO4. \n.\nUsual strengths. Rosuvastatin, 5 mg and Fenofibrate,\n160 mg; Rosuvastatin, 10 mg and Fenofibrate, 80 mg; \nRosuvastatin, 10 mg and Fenofibrate, 160 mg.\nIn the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c).\nDissolution (2.5.2). :\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), \n; \n-\nMedium, 900 ml of a solution, preparedbydissolving! O.g of \nsodium lauryLsulphate in 1000 ml of water,\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 60 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2A14), using the \nchromatographic system, solvent mixture and system \nsuitability criteria as described under Assay. 3\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.\nReference solution (a). A 0.052 per cent w/v solution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in solvent mixture;\nReference solution (b). A 0.18 per cent w/v solution of \nfenofibrate IPRS in solvent mixture.\nReferehce solution (c). Dilute a suitable volume of reference\nsolution (a) and (b) with dissolution medium, to obtain a \nsolution having concentration similar to the test solution.\nROSUVASIATINANl) FENOFIBRATE TABLETS\nCalculate the content of C22H28FN3O6S and C20H2)ClO4 in .the \nmedium. , \n. \n.. \n• \n/■-. ;• \n¡a.- ■\nQ. Not less than 70 per cent Of the stated amount of\ni's,: 1 -—■■■■ \" '' ■\nRelated su bstances. Determine:by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \nA: \nA-JÁ T- A.; -/AT\nUse chromatographic system and test solution as described \nunder Assay. .. \" -aáa?- t •->0.;.\nInject fhetest Solution. The-area of any secondary peak is hot \nmore than T.O per centandthe sum of areas of all thesecondary \npeaks is not more than 2.0 per cent, calculated by area \nnormalisation.\nUniformity of content. Complies with the test stated under \nTablets.- ,a^'2. \\?-,\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Disperse 1 tablet in 10 ml of water with the aid \nof ultrasound. Add about 30 ml o f solvent mixture arid disperse \nwith aid of ultrasound for 15 minutes. Further add 30 ml of \nmobile phase and disperse with aid of ultrasound for 25 \nminutes, cool and dilute to 10,0.0 ml with mobile phase, mix and\ncentrifuge at 2500 rpm for 10 minutes. Rèj ecting the first few \nml of filtrate, dilute 5.0 ml of the solution to 50.0 mlwith the \nmobilephase. -a-\"-’\nReference solution. A 0.012 per cent w/vsolution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in the solvent mixture and dilute \nto volume withniobile phase to obtainasolution having similar \nconcentration to the test solution. - \n; T ; \n, \n-\nUse the solvent mixture and chromatographic system \nas described under Assay. \n;, ;\nCalculate the content of C22H2&FN3O6S in the tablet. ....... ,, .\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.. .\nAssay; Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). \n; ’\nSolvent mixture. 50 volumes of methanol and 50 volumes of \nN,N-diamethylformamide.'' : \nir'!' ''■\nTest solution.: Weigh andpowder 20 tablets. Dispersé a \nquantity of powder containing 800 mg of Fenofibrate in\n125;mhof the solvent mixture, with-the aid of ultrasound fór \n25 minutes with intermittent shhkihg and dilute to250 ml with \nthe mobile phase,, mix and; centrifuge. Dilute 5.0 ml of clear \nsupernatant to 50.0 ml with the mobile phase. ,\nReference solution(a). i\\ 0.052 per cent w/v solution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in, the solvent .mixture. ;i\nReference solution(bf A. 0.064 per cent w/v solution of \nfenofibrate IPRS in the solvent mixture. \ni f ...\nReference solution (c). Dilute asui table volume of reference \nsolution (a) and; (b).'with;móbile phase, to obtain a solution \nhaving concentration similar to the test solution.\nIP202^J\n. .... ... ...... .. -—\nChromatographic sy"},"sections":[{"name":"CONTENT","text":"Rosuvastatin Calcium and Fenofibrate Tablets\nRosuvastatin. and Fenofibrate Tablets contain not less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated \namount of rosuvastatin, C22H28FN3O6S and fenofibrate, \nC20H2IClO4. \n.\nUsual strengths. Rosuvastatin, 5 mg and Fenofibrate,\n160 mg; Rosuvastatin, 10 mg and Fenofibrate, 80 mg; \nRosuvastatin, 10 mg and Fenofibrate, 160 mg.\nIn the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c).\nDissolution (2.5.2). :\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), \n; \n-\nMedium, 900 ml of a solution, preparedbydissolving! O.g of \nsodium lauryLsulphate in 1000 ml of water,\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 60 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2A14), using the \nchromatographic system, solvent mixture and system \nsuitability criteria as described under Assay. 3\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.\nReference solution (a). A 0.052 per cent w/v solution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in solvent mixture;\nReference solution (b). A 0.18 per cent w/v solution of \nfenofibrate IPRS in solvent mixture.\nReferehce solution (c). Dilute a suitable volume of reference\nsolution (a) and (b) with dissolution medium, to obtain a \nsolution having concentration similar to the test solution.\nROSUVASIATINANl) FENOFIBRATE TABLETS\nCalculate the content of C22H28FN3O6S and C20H2)ClO4 in .the \nmedium. , \n. \n.. \n• \n/■-. ;• \n¡a.- ■\nQ. Not less than 70 per cent Of the stated amount of\ni's,: 1 -—■■■■ \" '' ■\nRelated su bstances. Determine:by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \nA: \nA-JÁ T- A.; -/AT\nUse chromatographic system and test solution as described \nunder Assay. .. \" -aáa?- t •->0.;.\nInject fhetest Solution. The-area of any secondary peak is hot \nmore than T.O per centandthe sum of areas of all thesecondary \npeaks is not more than 2.0 per cent, calculated by area \nnormalisation.\nUniformity of content. Complies with the test stated under \nTablets.- ,a^'2. \\?-,\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Disperse 1 tablet in 10 ml of water with the aid \nof ultrasound. Add about 30 ml o f solvent mixture arid disperse \nwith aid of ultrasound for 15 minutes. Further add 30 ml of \nmobile phase and disperse with aid of ultrasound for 25 \nminutes, cool and dilute to 10,0.0 ml with mobile phase, mix and\ncentrifuge at 2500 rpm for 10 minutes. Rèj ecting the first few \nml of filtrate, dilute 5.0 ml of the solution to 50.0 mlwith the \nmobilephase. -a-\"-’\nReference solution. A 0.012 per cent w/vsolution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in the solvent mixture and dilute \nto volume withniobile phase to obtainasolution having similar \nconcentration to the test solution. - \n; T ; \n, \n-\nUse the solvent mixture and chromatographic system \nas described under Assay. \n;, ;\nCalculate the content of C22H2&FN3O6S in the tablet. ....... ,, .\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.. .\nAssay; Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). \n; ’\nSolvent mixture. 50 volumes of methanol and 50 volumes of \nN,N-diamethylformamide.'' : \nir'!' ''■\nTest solution.: Weigh andpowder 20 tablets. Dispersé a \nquantity of powder containing 800 mg of Fenofibrate in\n125;mhof the solvent mixture, with-the aid of ultrasound fór \n25 minutes with intermittent shhkihg and dilute to250 ml with \nthe mobile phase,, mix and; centrifuge. Dilute 5.0 ml of clear \nsupernatant to 50.0 ml with the mobile phase. ,\nReference solution(a). i\\ 0.052 per cent w/v solution of \nrosuvastatin calcium IPRS in, the solvent .mixture. ;i\nReference solution(bf A. 0.064 per cent w/v solution of \nfenofibrate IPRS in the solvent mixture. \ni f ...\nReference solution (c). Dilute asui table volume of reference \nsolution (a) and; (b).'with;móbile phase, to obtain a solution \nhaving concentration similar to the test solution.\nIP202^J\n. .... ... ...... .. -—\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with A\n. octadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 40» volumes of a buffer I\nsolution prepared by dissolving 0.77 g of ammoniuni-\n! acetate, add 5 ml of triethyfamine and pH adjusted to\n4.0 with brthophosphoric acid in '■ 1000 ml of water 60 It \nvolumes of acetonitrile, ; \n, ;\n- flow rate: a gradient programme using the conditions É\ngiven below, \n»... . \n/p. \n; U\nTime \nFlow • \n. \n®\n(in min.) \n, (ml) \n; \nhf\n0.0- . \n: \nf\n7.0 \n0.7\n8.0 \n2.0\n35.0 \n2.0\n36.0 \n0.7\n40.0 \n0.7\n- spectrophotometer set at 240 nm, -\n- injection volume:.20 pl.\nInject reference solution (c). The test is not valid unless \nthe relative standard deviation of replicate injections for each \npeaks is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject reference solution (c) and the test solution^ J\nCalculate the content of CWIL^FN^OèS and C20H2ÎCIÔ4 mthè \ntablets. \n.... \n■■■ -.aàa'aaà.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture at a temperature below\n3(T. . \n-Ar./\nLabellin g. The label states the strength in terms of the \nequivalent amount of rosuvastatin, arid fenofibrate."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/rosuvastatin-calcium","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Rosuvastatin Calcium"},"edition":"ip-