ntubes containing the, sample dilutions. Add 1 ml -of enzyme \nsolution to all these tubes and vertex the tubes, for exactly IQ \nseconds. Keep the test tubes in the water-bath at .37° for 20 \nminutes for the reaction. After exactly 20 minutes, add 5 ml of \nTCA to tubes marked as test and 5 ml of Casein substrate to \nthe tube marked as blank Vortex all the tubes exactly for 30 \nseconds. Keep the tubes in the water-bath at 37Q for 30 minutes \nfor precipitation, filter. \n!■ j:-j ■.. ■\nReference solution (a). A 0.4 per cent w/v solution of \nsertaconazole n itrate IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). A 0.4 per cent w/v solution of\n1-\nSertaconazole Nitrate\nmiconazole nitrate IPRS in reference solution (a).\nApply to the plate 5 pl of each solution. Allow the mobile \nphase to rise 15 cm. After development, dry the plate in air for\ni\n15 minutes and expose to iodine vapour for 30 minutes. The \nprincipal spot in the chromatogram obtained with the test\nsolution corresponds to that in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (a). The spot in the,chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (b) shows 2 clearly separated \nspots.\nNOTE—For tablets, the settlement may take a longer time\nthan 30 minutes. So filter the solution after the settlement is \nclearly seen (Vortex in between for better precipitation).\nE. It gives the reactions of nitrates (2.3.1).\nMark tubes as test, blank, tyrosine and tyrosine blank."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Mol.Wt.500.8\nAdd the following respectively; \n.. .\nAppearance of solution. A 1.0 per cent w/v solution in ethanol \n(95 percent) is clear (2.4.1), and not more intensely coloured \nthan reference solution YS5 (2.4.1).\nSertaconazole Nitrate is (RS)-1 -[2-[(7-Chloro-l -benzothiophen- \n3-yl)rhfetKdxJ^2-'(2,4-dichlorophenyl)ethyl]-1 H-imidazole\nTest-2 ml of the test filtrate.\nnitrate. ,;AA.r;L>\nBlank-2 ml of blank filtrate. \nm m\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nSertaconazoleNitrate contains not less than 98,5 per cent and \nnot more than 101.0 per cent of C2fU A ANT) ■ S calculated on \nthe anhydrous basis.\nTyrosine - 2 ml of tyrosine standard solution.\nTyrosine blank-0.2 M hydrochloric acid.\nTest solution. Dissolve 10 mg of the substance under \nexamination in the mobile phase and dilute to 10.0 ml with the \nmobile phase.\nAdd 5 ml of 6 per cent sodium carbonate solution to all tubes.\nCategory. Antifungal.\nAdd 1 ml of diluted Folin’s reagent to all the tubes. Keep the \ntubes at 37° for 30 minutes for colour development. Measure \nthe absorbance at about 660 nm (2.4.7).\nDescription. A white or almost white powder.\nReference solution (a). Dilute 5.0 ml of the test solution to\n100.0 ml with the mobile phase. Dilute 1.0 ml ofthe solution to \n20.0 ml with the mobile phase."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Test A and C may be omitted if tests B, D and E are carried \nouL Tes ts B, D and E may be omitted if test A and C are\nA — A \nT ■\nSerratiopeptidase Units/Tablet - —!------~ x 176 x —— *\nReference solution (b). A solution containing 0.0005 per cent\n- . . . . : 1 TOO \n25 TOO \n'\n— x--------- x — x-----------x Avg. wt. in g\nA3-A4 \n0.160\nw/v each of sertaconazole nitrateIPRSand miconazole nitrate \nIPRS in the mobile phase.\ncarried out.. >\nA. Meltingpoint (2.4.21). 156° to 161°.\n20 Spl.wl.(g) \n5 \n2\nChromatographic system\nB. When examined in the range 240 nm to 320 nm (2.4.7), a 0.01\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.0 mm, packed with\nper cèht w/Vsbliition in methanol gives absorption maxima at \n-60 nm, 293 nm and 302 nm and the absorbance ratio \n(Ajœ/A^) is 1.1610 1;28.\nnitrile silica (10 pm),\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 37 volumes of acetonitrile\nPercentage of L.A - Serratiopeptidase Units/Tablet * jqq\n■ \n••• \n■■ L.A. \n■.\nand 63 volumes a buffer solution prepared by dissolving\nwhere, !76 = Conversion Co-efficient of Tyrosine to\n1.5 g of sodium dihydrogen phosphate in 1000 ml of \nwater.\nDetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with sertaconazole\nSerratiopeptidase,\n3570\n3571\nwww.webofpharma.com\nSERTACONAZOLE NITRATE\n. - flowrate: 1.6 ml per minute, .\n- spectrophotometer set at 220 nm,\n- \ninjectionvolume: 20pl. \n, :.........\nThe retention time of peaks due to nitrate ion is about 1 minute, \nmiconazole about 17 minutes and sertaconazole about 19\nminutes. ; \n; \n. •••\nInject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to miconazole and \nsertaconazole is not less than 2,0.\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 1.3 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. In the chromatogram obtained with the test solution, \nthe area of any peak corresponding sertaconazole impurity A; \nB and C are hot more than the'areao f the principalpeak in the \nchromatogram obtained, with reference solution (a) (Q.25 per \ncent), the relative retention,time of impurity C, impurity B and \nimpurityAare about 0.12,0.18 and 0.3 respectively, thesum of \nthe areas of all the secondary peaks is not more than twice the \narea of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nréférencé'solution (aj (0.5 per cent); Ignore ânÿ peak which is \n0.2 times the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solutioh (a) (0.05 per ceht) arid düé to \niiitraté ion. ; ; \n\"■ - ■■ \n’• \n',:-\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 percent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 1.0 per,cent, determined, on\n0.5g.\nAssay. Dissolve 0.4 g in 50 ml mixture of equal volumes of \nanhydrous acetic acid and methyl .ethyl ketone. Titrate with \n0.Ï M perchloric acid, determining the end-point \npotentiometrically (2.4.25). Carry put a blank titration.\n1 ml of 0.1 Mperchloric acid is equivalent to 0.05008 g of\nStorage. Store protected from light."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/sertraline-hydrochloride-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Sertraline Hydrochloride Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Sertraline Hydrochloride Tablets\nSertraline Tablets contain noticss than .95.0 per cent and not \nmore than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of sertraline, \nc17hi7ci2n. .:. ■' \\ \n’- ;..\nUsual strength. 25 mg; 50 mg; lOOmg."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Sertraline Hydrochloride Tablets\nSertraline Tablets contain noticss than .95.0 per cent and not \nmore than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of sertraline, \nc17hi7ci2n. .:. ■' \\ \n’- ;..\nUsual strength. 25 mg; 50 mg; lOOmg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Shake a quantity of thè powdered tablets containing 0.25 gof \nSertraline Hydrochloride with 10 ini of ethdh'olffx TO minutes, \nfilter and evaporate the filtrate to dryness. On the residue, \ndetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4,6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with sertraline \nhydrochloride ¿RRS or with the reference spectrum of sertraline \nhydrochloride. ■ ."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Apparatus No; 2 (Paddle), ;\nMedium. 900 ml of sodium acetate buffer solution pH 4.5,:\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 30 minutes. ; \n;\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Use the filtrate as given above.\nReference solution. A solution of sertraline hydrochloride\nIP RSof the concentration similar to the test solution in the \ndissolution medium. ’ ? •>. : : : \\ T\nIf 2022\nChromatographic system ■: \n1 - hLm-rr\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 nun,packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (4.prn),,\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 15; volumes Of methanol\n; 40 volumes of a solution containing 0.286 percent v/v\nglacial acetic acid and 0.348 per cent vlvhffthylantine\nand 45 volumes of acetonitrile, \n.7’\n- flow rate: 1.8 ml per minute, ’\n- spectrophotometer set at 265 nm, \n?;\n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nCalculate the content of Ci7Hi7C12N in the medium.\nQ. Not less than 75 per cent of the stated amount of CJ7H17C12N.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). •’\nSolvent mixture. 30 volumes of acetonitrile and 70 volumes \nofw/er. \n’ \n'y.-.\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of whole tablets containing \n500 mg of Sertraline Hydrochloride with 150 ml of the solvent \nmixture with the aid of ultrasound and dilute to 200 ml with the \nsolvent mixture and filter. \n.. •; u ? • a,v: :\nReference solution (a): Dilute 1.0 ml of the test Solution to\n500.0 ml with the solvent mixture. \n' ’1 •.\nReference solution (b). A 0.001 per cent w/v solution of\n(fffmandelic acid (sertraline impurity, E) in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (c). A 0;25 per cent w/vj solution of \nsertraline hydrochloride impurity IPRS in solvent mixture..\nReference solution (d). Dilute 1.0 mlof reference ..solution (a) \nto 2.0 mlwith the solvent mixture.,,.\nChromatographic system \n’’\n' - a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 jufri),\n- mobile phase: A. a. 0.272 per cent w/v solution of\npotassium dihydrogeh orthophosphate, adjusted to pH\n3.0 with ortho phosphoric acid,\nB. acetonitrile, \n■.\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute.\n- spectrophotometer set at 210 nm, \n; : -\n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n70 .\n30\n30\n70\n30\n40 \n■\n60\n40\n41\n.7°\n, ' 30\n51\n70 - ■\n. : ’ •• 30 ...;\n3576\nwww.webofpharma.com\n. t referencc solution (c). For peak identification of \n‘\"^linehydrochlomleimpunly. \n/\nI ect reference solution (a), (b), (d) and the. test solution. In \nthe chromatogram \nthe test solution, the area of\nvpà corresponding to sertraline impurity C ( lRS,4RS)-4- \nM-chlóf oph