.7 ml per minute,\n\"Spectrophotometer set at210nm, \n~ injection volume: 40 pl."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Inject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the \nRelationbetween .the two principal peaks is not less than"},{"name":"Tests","text":"Inject reference solution (a) and the test solution. In the\nc omatogrami obtained with the test solution, the area of any\nSILDENAFIL CITRATE\npeak corresponding to sertraline cis-isomer is not more than \nthe area of the principal peak in the; chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (a) (1.5 per cent).\nOther tests.1 Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 'tablets! Disperse a quantity \nof the powder containing 0.2 g of Sertraline Hydrochloride \nwith 150 ml of the mobile phase with the aid of ultrasound for \n45 minutes, cool and dilute to 200 ml with water, filter. Dilute \n5 .0 ml of the solution to 100.0 ml with the mobile phase.\nReference solution. A0.005 per cent w/v solution of sertraline \nhydrochloride IPRS in the mobile phase.:\nUse chromatographic system as described under Dissolution.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of Cl7H]7Cl2N, in the tablets.\nSildenafil Citrate\no\nC^HjMOhS ; \n' \n/. Mol. Wt. 666.7\nSildenafil Citrate is 5-[2-ethoxy-5-(4-methylpiperazinyl- \nsulphonyl)phenyl]-l-methyl-3-«-propyl-1,6-dihydro- \n7#-pyrazolo[4,3-<7]pyrimidin-7-one citrate.\nSildenafil Citrate contains not less than 98.0 per cent and not \nmore than 102.0 per cent of C28H3gN6O[]S, calculated on the \nanhydrous basis.\nCategory. Used in erectile dysfunction.\nDescription. A white to off white powder.\nDetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompiare the spectrum that obtained with sildenafil citrate \nIPRS or with the reference spectrum of sildenafil citrate.\nCitricacid. 28.0 per centto 34.0 per cent.\nWeigh 0.2 g of the substance under ex