of the substance under \nexamination in the solvent mixture and dilute to 250.0 ml with \nthe solvent mixture. ”' ‘ \n’ \n•■■■■■\nReference solution (a). A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of \nsitagliptin phosphate IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a); \nto 100.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (c). In order to prepare sitagliptin fumarate\nadduct in-situ, place 10 mg of sitagliptinphosphate IPRS and\n1 mgof sodium stearyl fumarate in a vial, add 1 ml of water \narid tightly seal the vial.' Heat at 80° for 48 hours. Transfer the \ncontents of the vial into a 100-ml volumetric flask using a \nsmall amount of the solvent mixture. Rinse the vial three times \nwith the solvent mixture. Transfer the rinsates into the flask \nand dilute to 100.0 ml with the solvent mixture, and centrifuge. \nUse the supernatant liquid.\nChromatographic system\n—; a column 1.5, cm x 4.6 mm packed with endcapped\n• cyanopropyl si lane bonded to porous silica (5. pm), \n- mobile phase: a mixture, of 15 volumes of acetonitrile.\nand 85 volumes of a buffer solution prepared by \ndissolving 1.36 g of potassium' dihydro'gen phosphate\nJ in about 900 ml of water, adjusted to pH 2.0 with\northophosphoric acid and dilute to 1000 ml with 'water, \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, ' \np’\n- spectrophotometer set at 205 nm,\ninjection volume: 20 pl. \n,\nThe relative retention time with reference to the sitagliptin \npeak for the fumarate adduct is about 1.2. ,\nInject reference solution (c). The test is hot valid unless the \nresolution between sitagliptin and the fumarate adduct is not \nless than 1.0. \n?/wrww-nrw:\nInject reference solution (a), (b) and the test solution.Ruq^ j \nchromatogram 5 times the retention time of the principal peak i \nIn the chromatogram obtained with the test solution^ the area ■ I \nof any. secondary peak is not more than 0.1 times tire area of I \nthe principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with ref