utions (b) and (c). The test is not valid \nunless the column efficiency determined from the thymine, \nstavudine and lamivudine peaks is not less than 3000 theoretical \nplates and the tailing factor for the same peaks is not more \nthan 2.0.\nStavudine and Lamivudine Tablets contain not less than I \n90.0 per cent and not more than 1'10.0 per cent of the sta | \namounts of stavudine, C10H.2M2O4 and lainivu me. |\n1'5 and the relative standard deviation for replicate inj ections\neach of the peaks corresponding to stavudine and \nbmivudine is not more than 1.0 per cent.\nC8HhN3O3S. \n.\nUsual strengths. Stavudine, 30 mg and Lamivudine, 150^ |\ninject the reference solution and the test solution and measure \ntlie responses for the major peaks due to stavudine and\nInject water and the test solution. Examine the chromatogram \nobtained with water for any extraneous peaks and ignore the \ncorresponding peaks observed in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution.\nStavudine, 40 mg. and Lamivudine, 150 mg.\n¡aniivudine."},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the two principal peaks in the chromatog^® ! \nobtained with the test solution correspond to the \n|\nto stavudine and lamivudine in the chromatogram 0 ta\nAcúlate the contents of C!0H32N2O4and CgHuNjOaS in the\nAny secondary peak observed in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponding to thymine is not more \nthan 3.0 per cent. Any other secondary peak observed in the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution is not more\nmedium.\nQ- Not less than 70 per cent of the stated amounts of \nCisHnN^andCsHn^OaS.\nwith the reference solution.\n3659\nwww.webofpharma.com\nSTAVUDINE AND LAMIVUDINE TABLETS\nthan 0.5 per cent and the sum ofthe areas of :all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 4.0 per cent when calculated, by \npercentagearcanormalisation. \n7.\nOther tests-jComply with :the tests stated under Tablets. / >\nAssay; Determiné'by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). 1\nTe