time with reference to tadalafil for \n6R,12aS diastereomer is about 1.03.\nInject reference solution (a) and (b). The test is not valid unless \nthe tailing factor is not more than 1.5 in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (a) and signal-to-noise ratio \nis not less than 10 in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b). \n. .. ;\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.1 \nper cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary peaks\nis not more than 3 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.3 per \ncent). Ignore any peak with an area less than 0.5 times the area \nof the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (a) (0.05 per cent). Ignore the peaks due to \nthe 6R, 12aS and 6S, 12aR diastereomers of tadalafil, which co­\nelute at a retention time of about 1.03 relative to. tadalafil.\nLoss on drying (2.4.19).Not more than 0.5 per cent, determined \non 1 g by drying under vacuum at 105° for 3 hours.\ni\n3\n37Ó7\nwww.webofpharma.com\nTADALAFIL\nSulphatedash (2.3 J 8). Not morethan 0.1 per cent, a - -fi. , i ,=.-?\nAssay: Determine by Iiquidchromatography(2.4.r4).iV1'/ \"\nwdter. ■i ■-\n1 ;>.:■■■ \nh lii i \ni ■ i (1 d'.A; \nm \n\"'U A ■ I U.U 5 h r(\nSolution A. Add 1.0 ml of trifluorodcetic acid to 1000 ml of\nTest.splutiom Dissolve a quantity of the substance under \nexamination ina mixture of equal volumes of acetonitrile and \nsolution A, prepared by first dissolving in acetonitrile and \nthen dilute"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/talcum","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Talcum"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"; Talcum \n:\nTest solution, jUse the filtrate, dilute if necessary', \ndissolution medium.\nPowdered, selected, natural, hydrated magnesium silicate. Pure \ntalc has the formula Mg3Si4O10(()H)2. It may contain variable \namounts of associated minerals among which chlorites \n(hydrated aluminium and magnesium silicates), magnesite \n(magnesium;,carbonate),, calcite (calcium^carbonate) \nand dolomite (calcium and magnesium carbonate) are \npredominant.\nsolution-\nReference solution. A0.025 perbent w/v solution of \nIPRS in a mixture of'equal volumes of acetonitrile and:k^\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets,\nDilute a volume of the solution with, the dissolution \nto obtain 0.0075 mgperml oltadalafilIPRS. \n;\n¿¿say. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nEqual volumes of acetonitrile and water. :\nChromatographic system\nTestsolution; Place hot less thah 20 tablets into an appropriate \nsize volumetric flask. Fill the flask about50 per cent with the \nsolvent mixture anddisperse with the aid of ultrasound and \ndilute with the solvent mixture to volume. Allow the solution \nto stand for i hour. Dilute the solution, if necessary to obtain \na solution containing 0.25 mg per ml of Tadalafil. Centrifuge or \nfilter the solution. (NOTE — The initial concentration before \na secondary dilution step should-not exceed? 6 mg per ml).-\n•L'-rrv- a stainless steel column 5 cm x 4.6 mm, packed ^ \noctylsilane bonded to porous silicaf 3.5 uni), i ÿi -jW\nCategory. Pharmaceutical aid (dusting powder).\nDescription. A white or almost.white, powder, free from \ngrittiness; readily adheres to the skin; unctuous to the \ntOUch. ’ ' ' . j ...\n- \ncolumntemperature:40°. \n3..??\n- mobile phase: a mixture of equal volumes of methanol\nand water, \n.-..-ur m ¡- . v ¡ v-AC\n- flow rate: 2 ml per minute, \n-i>. .^ ■.:?\n- spectrophotometer set at 225 nm, . J v. a y \n- injection volume: 50 pl. \n......... -“Sy,"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"; Talcum \n:\nTest solution, jUse the filtrate, dilute if necessary', \ndissolution medium.\nPowdered, selected, natural, hydrated magnesium silicate. Pure \ntalc has the formula Mg3Si4O10(()H)2. It may contain variable \namounts of associated minerals among which chlorites \n(hydrated aluminium and magnesium silicates), magnesite \n(magnesium;,carbonate),, calcite (calcium^carbonate) \nand dolomite (calcium and magnesium carbonate) are \npredominant.\nsolution-\nReference solution. A0.025 perbent w/v solution of \nIPRS in a mixture of'equal volumes of acetonitrile and:k^\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets,\nDilute a volume of the solution with, the dissolution \nto obtain 0.0075 mgperml oltadalafilIPRS. \n;\n¿¿say. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nEqual volumes of acetonitrile and water. :\nChromatographic system\nTestsolution; Place hot less thah 20 tablets into an appropriate \nsize volumetric flask. Fill the flask about50 per cent with the \nsolvent mixture anddisperse with the aid of ultrasound and \ndilute with the solvent mixture to volume. Allow the solution \nto stand for i hour. Dilute the solution, if necessary to obtain \na solution containing 0.25 mg per ml of Tadalafil. Centrifuge or \nfilter the solution. (NOTE — The initial concentration before \na secondary dilution step should-not exceed? 6 mg per ml).-\n•L'-rrv- a stainless steel column 5 cm x 4.6 mm, packed ^ \noctylsilane bonded to porous silicaf 3.5 uni), i ÿi -jW\nCategory. Pharmaceutical aid (dusting powder).\nDescription. A white or almost.white, powder, free from \ngrittiness; readily adheres to the skin; unctuous to the \ntOUch. ’ ' ' . j ...\n- \ncolumntemperature:40°. \n3..??\n- mobile phase: a mixture of equal volumes of methanol\nand water, \n.-..-ur m ¡- . v ¡ v-AC\n- flow rate: 2 ml per minute, \n-i>. .^ ■.:?\n- spectrophotometer set at 225 nm, . J v. a y \n- injection volume: 50 pl. \n......... -“Sy,"},{"name":"Production","text":"Talc derived from deposits that are known to contain associated \nasbestos is not suitable for pharmaceutical pse; The \nmanufacturer is responsible for demonstrating by thqtest for \namphiboles and serpentines that the product is free from \nasbestos. ’\n■ The presence of amphiboles and of serpentines is \nrevealed by infrared spectrophotometry. If detected, the \nspecific; morphological criteria of asbéstos are investigated \nby a suitable method of optical microscopy to: determine \nwhether tremolite asbestos 6r chrysotile is'present, as \ndescribed below.\nReference solution (a). A 0.025 per cent w/v solution of \ntadalafil IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 1.5 and the relative standard\nReference solution '(b). To partially convert tadalafil to the \n6R,12aSdiastereomer. transfer 25 ml of the reference'solution \nintota suitable container. Add 0.25 ml of 5 A/sodium-hydroxide, \nmixwelfand let stand for 30 minutes,Neutralize the solution \ntopH7 by drop-wise addition of'trifluoroacetic acid. (NOTE—■ \nTluf solution is stable for I month when stored in a \nrejrigerdtor).\ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0.\nQ. Not less than 40 per cent of the stated amount of C^HuNjtk \nat 10 minutes and not less than 80 per cent of the stated \namount ofC22H19N3O4 at 30 minutes. \nTA/j\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4,14) as described under Assay with the following\nI I \n■I\nmodifications. ■\nChromatographic system \n;\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\nDetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometiy (2.4.6).\nThe relative retention timé with reference to tadalafil for \n6R,12aS diastereomer oftadaiafil is abouti .2.! \n;\n\"< octylsilane bonded to porous silica (3.5 pm),\nIn the .range 740 cm1 to 76,0- cm 1 using scale expansion, any \nabsorption band: at 758 cm' 1 -may indicate the presence of \ntremolite or of chlorite. Ifthe absorption bandremainsafter \nignition of the substance under examination at 85 O.± 50° for at \nleast 30 minutes, it indie ate sthe presence of the tremolite. In \nthe range 600 cm-1 to 650 cm 1 using scale expansion, any \nabsorption band or shoulder may indicate the presence of \nserpentines. \n\"< \n' '■ N' ^’0 — - '\n- column temperature: 35°, \n’ 1 :\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 35 volumes of acetonitrile,\nInject reference solution (a) and (b). The test is not valid tiniest\nI\nthe tailing factor is not more than 1.5 in the chromatogram\n65 volumes of water and 0,1 volume of trifluoroacetic \nacid, . ..\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 285 nm,\n- injection volume: 10 ul.\nobtained with reference solution (a) and the resolution \nbetween the peaks due to tadalafil and the 6R, 12aS diastereomer \npeák'is 'nÓt I'ess than 3.O 'in the chromatogram obtained with\nreference solution (b). \n' \n■■■■■\nInj ect the test solution. The area-of any secondary peak is not | \nmore than; 0.2 per icent and, the sum of the areas of all thfe< |"},{"name":"Identification","text":"; : \nr io\nThe relative retention time with reference to tadalafil for \n6R,12aS diastereomer is about 1.2. \n, : ;\nsecondary peaks is not more, than 0,3 per cent. Ignore any .| \npeak with an area less the 0,05 per cent, calculated by area |\nTest A may be omitted if tests B, C are carried out.Tests B and \nC may be omitted if test A is carried out. ; ; v '\nlnj^c(reference solution (a) and (b). The test is not valid unless \n^solution between the peaks due to tadalafil and the 6R ,12aS \ndiastereomer peak is not less than 3.0 in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (b) and the tailing factor is\nnormalization method. \n.. \n\\\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6), \nshows absorption bands at 3677 ^2 cm'1,1018 ± 2 cm'1 and \n669±2cnrl. \n: v'' r t;:' \n: ’\nUniformity of content1. Complies with the test stated undéf | \nTablets. \n|\n' .■ , .. .... . ; ■ ■■ \n■ \n. : \n■■ I\nSolvent mixturé. Equ