 ,\nIron (2,3.14). Boil 4.0 g with 25 ml of water for 30 minutes, \nreplacing the water lost by evaporation, arid filter. The filtrate, \nafter the addition of 5 ml of nitric acid, complies with'the limit \ntest for iron (10 ppm)? \n■■ J\nAcid-soluble substances. Not more than 2.0 per cent, \ndetermined, by the following method, Digest 2.0 g with 40 ml of \ndilute hydrochloric acid for 15 minutes, filter, evaporate the \nfiltrate; tp the residue add 0.1 ml of sulphuric, acid and ignite \nat 800 - 25<! to constant weight. . ,.\nWater-soluble substances. To 10 g add 50 ml of carbon \ndioxide-free water, heat to boiling and maintain boiling under \na reflux condenser for 3Ó minutes. Allow to cool, filter through \na medium-speed filter paper and diluteto 50.0 ml with carbon \ndioxide-free water. Take 25 ml of the filtrate, evaporate to \ndryness and heat at; 105° for 1 hour. The residue weighs a \nmaximum of 10 mg. \n- m ; \n'\nCarbonates. To 1 g add 20 ml of dilute hydrochloric acid;, no \neffervescence is produced. / \n' \"\nChlorides (2.3.12). Suspend 2.0 g in 10 ml of water, add\n10 ml of 2 Mnitric acid, shake for 15 minutes and filter. 10 ml \nof the filtrate complies with the limit test Tor chlorides \n(250 ppm).\nOrganic compounds. The residue obtained in the test for Loss \non drying is not more than slightly yellow or grey.\nLoss on drying (2.4.19). Not more than. 1.0 per cent, determined \non 1.0 g by drying in an oven at 180° for Í hour.\nMicrobial contamination (frfrfr). If intended for topical \napplication, the total aerobic viable, count is not more than. 102 \nCFUper g. I f intended for oral administration, the total aerobic \nviable count is not more than 1O3 ÇFU .per g and total fungal \ncount is not more than 1O2 ÇFÜ per. g. \n, \n.XX'-\nStorage. Store protected from moisture. \nh <•'.\nIP2022\nTALG"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tamoxifen-citrate-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tamoxifen Citrate Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Tamoxifen Citrate Tablets \n,\nTamoxifen Tablets contain hot less than 90.0 per cent and not \nmore than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of tamoxifen, \nC26ll29NO. . . \n... \n... \n.\nUsual strengths: The equivalent of 10 mg, 20 mg and 40 mg of \ntamoxifen.1 ■. \n•."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Tamoxifen Citrate Tablets \n,\nTamoxifen Tablets contain hot less than 90.0 per cent and not \nmore than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of tamoxifen, \nC26ll29NO. . . \n... \n... \n.\nUsual strengths: The equivalent of 10 mg, 20 mg and 40 mg of \ntamoxifen.1 ■. \n•."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Tests B and C may be omitted if tests A and D are carried out. \nTest A . may be omitted if tests B, C and D are carried put.,\nA. To a quantity of the powdered tablets containing 0,1 g of \nTamoxifen add 20 ml of water, warm, add 2 ml of 5 M sodium \nhydroxide and cool. Extract with two quantities, each of 10 ml, \nof ether, filtering after each extraction. Combine the ether \nextracts and evaporate to dryness in a stream of nitrogen at \nroom temperature. Diy the residue at a pressure not exceeding \n0.7 kPa for 30 minutes.\nOn the residue, determine by infrared absorption \nspectrophotometry (2.4.6). Compare the spectrum with \nthat obtained with tamoxifen citrate IPRS treated in the \nsame manner or with the reference spectrum of tamoxifen.\nB. When examined in the range 220 nm to 360 nm (2;4.7), a \n0.002 per cent w/v solution in methanol ofthe residue obtained \nin test A shows absorption maxima at about 237 nm and \n275 nm\nC. Determine by thin-layer chromatography (2,4.17), coating \nthe plate with silica gel GF254.\nMobile phase. A mixture of TOO volumes of ethyl acetate,\n10 volumes of methanol and 1 volume of strong ammonia \nsolution. ■\nTAMOXIFEN. TABLETS\nTest isolations. Shake ; a quantityofthe powdered ^tablets \ncontaining 0.1 < g?Tamoxifehlwith::lOEml * o&methanof ■. filter