lent to 0.05636 g of\nC161-119N0, C611807.\nC26H29NO,C6H807 \t\nMol. Wt. 563.7\nChromatographic system\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nTamoxifen Citrate is (Z)-2-[4-(1,2-diphenylbut-l-eny1)-\na stainless steel column 20 cm x 5 mm, packed with \noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), \nmobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of acetonitrile, \n25 volumes of water, 15 volumes of tetrahydrofilran \nand 0.4 volume of strong ammonia solution, \nflow rate: 1.5 ml per minute, \nspectrophotometer set at 240 nm, \ninjection volume: 20 pl.\n1- phenoxy]ethyldimethylamine citrate.\nTamoxifen Citrate contains not less than 99.0 per cent and not \nmore than 101.0 per cent of C26H29NO, C 6H807, calculatedio\nTamoxifen Tablets\n the dried basis."},"sections":[{"name":"TAMOXIFEN TABLETS","text":"0, 20 18\nTamoxifen Citrate\nSolven t mixture. 60 volumes of acetonitrile, 25 volumes of\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.2 per cent.\nwater and 15 volumes of tetrahydrofuran.\nLoss on drying (2.4.19). Not more than 0.5 per cent, determined \non 1.0 g by drying in an oven at 105°.\nN C H3\nu3iL;\nTest solution. Dissolve 0.25 g of the substance under \nexamination in 100 ml of solvent mixture\nAssay. Dissolve 1.0 g in 150 ml of anhydrous glacial acetic \nacid. Titrate with 0.1 M perchloric acid, using 1-naphthol-\nbenzein solution as indicator. Carry out a blank titration.\n6H3\nHO COON\nReference solution (a). A 0.0025 per cent w/v solution of the \nsubstance under examination in the solvent mixture.\nHOOC \t\nCOIN.\nReference solution (b). A 0.25 per cent w/v solution of \ntamoxifen citrate impurity standard RS in the solvent mixture.\n1 ml of 0.1 M perchloric acid is equivalent to 0.05636 g of\nC161-119N0, C611807.\nC26H29NO,C6H807 \t\nMol. Wt. 563.7\nChromatographic system\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nTamoxifen Citrate is (Z)-2-[4-(1,2-diphenylbut-l-eny1)-\na stainless steel column 20 cm x 5 mm, packed with \noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), \nmobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of acetonitrile, \n25 volumes of water, 15 volumes of tetrahydrofilran \nand 0.4 volume of strong ammonia solution, \nflow rate: 1.5 ml per minute, \nspectrophotometer set at 240 nm, \ninjection volume: 20 pl.\n1- phenoxy]ethyldimethylamine citrate.\nTamoxifen Citrate contains not less than 99.0 per cent and not \nmore than 101.0 per cent of C26H29NO, C 6H807, calculatedio\nTamoxifen Tablets\n the dried basis."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tamsulosin-hydrochloride-prolonged-release-and-dutasteride-capsules","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tamsulosin Hydrochloride Prolonged-release and Dutasteride Capsules"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TAMSULOSIN HYDROCHLORIDE PROLONGED-RELEASE AND DUTASTERIDE CAPSULES\nAssay. Determine by.liquid chromatography (2.4.44).\nNOTE — Use fresh ly prepared solutions. \n\" ' \" \" ' ‘ :\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of the mixed contents bf 20 \ncapsules containing 1.6 mg of Tamsulosin Hydrochloride in \n50, ml of 1 /M methanolic hydrochloric acid with'.the aid. of \nultrasound for 15 minutes and dilute to 100.0 ml with 2 .M \nmethanolic hydrochloric acid, filter using a 0.7-pm glass fibre \nfilter. Dilute 1 volume of the filtrate to 4 volumes with .1 ,M \nmethanolic hydrochloric acid. -\nReference solution. A Q.04 per cent w/v solution of tamsulosin \nhydrochloride TPRS in methanol with the aid of ultrasound. \nDilute I volume to 100 volumes with 1 M methanolic \nhydrochloric acid. ; \n-\nUse chromatographic system as described under Related \nsubstances. \n>• •• -■ '\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C20H28N2O5S,HCl in the capsules.\nTamsulosin Hydrochloride Prolonged- \nrelease and Dutasteride Capsules\nTamsulosin Hydrochloride Prolonged-release and \nDutasteride Capsules manufactured by different manufacture,\nwhilst complying with the requirements of the monograph \nare not interchangeable, as the dissolution profilé of the \nproducts of different, manufactures may not be the same.,\nTamsulosin hydrochloride Prolonged - release and.Dutasteride \nCapsules contain not less than 90.0 per cent and not more \nthan 110.0 per cent of the stated amounts of tamsulosin \nhydrochloride, C2oH28N205S,HC1\"and\" dutasteride,\nUsual strength. Dutasteride, 0.5 mg and Tamsulosin \nHydrochloride 0.4 mg."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TAMSULOSIN HYDROCHLORIDE PROLONGED-RELEASE AND DUTASTERIDE CAPSULES\nAssay. Determine by.liquid chromatography (2.4.44).\nNOTE — Use fresh ly prepared solutions. \n\" ' \" \" ' ‘ :\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of the mixed contents bf 20 \ncapsules containing 1.6 mg of Tamsulosin Hydrochloride in \n50, ml of 1 /M methanolic hydrochloric acid with'.the aid. of \nultrasound for 15 minutes and dilute to 100.0 ml with 2 .M \nmethanolic hydrochloric acid, filter using a 0.7-pm glass fibre \nfilter. Dilute 1 volume of the filtrate to 4 volumes with .1 ,M \nmethanolic hydrochloric acid. -\nReference solution. A Q.04 per cent w/v solution of tamsulosin \nhydrochloride TPRS in methanol with the aid of ultrasound. \nDilute I volume to 100 volumes with 1 M methanolic \nhydrochloric acid. ; \n-\nUse chromatographic system as described under Related \nsubstances. \n>• •• -■ '\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C20H28N2O5S,HCl in the capsules.\nTamsulosin Hydrochloride Prolonged- \nrelease and Dutasteride Capsules\nTamsulosin Hydrochloride Prolonged-release and \nDutasteride Capsules manufactured by different manufacture,\nwhilst complying with the requirements of the monograph \nare not interchangeable, as the dissolution profilé of the \nproducts of different, manufactures may not be the same.,\nTamsulosin hydrochloride Prolonged - release and.Dutasteride \nCapsules contain not less than 90.0 per cent and not more \nthan 110.0 per cent of the stated amounts of tamsulosin \nhydrochloride, C2oH28N205S,HC1\"and\" dutasteride,\nUsual strength. Dutasteride, 0.5 mg and Tamsulosin \nHydrochloride 0.4 mg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. In the Assay of dutasteride, the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution corresponds to \nthe peak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference \nsolution.\nB. In the Assay of tamsulosin; hydrochloride, the principal \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with the test: solution \ncorresponds to the chromatogram obtained with the reference \nsolution. \n... \n■ ;\nDissolution (2.5.2). Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \n- •; \n■ ... ••\nTAMSÜLOSIN HYDROCHLORIDE PROLONGED-RELEASE AND’ DUTASTERIDE CAPSULES\nFor tamsiilosih hydrochloride. Complies with the test stated \nunder Tablets. ..\nForDiitasteridy - \n.l:\\. \n,;.J, . \n..\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), ; n n ; r \nMédium. 500 ml of a buffer solution prepared by dissolving \n2.0 gmf sodium' chloride, and 7.0 m\\hydrochloric acid in \n800 ml of water and add 5.0 g of sodium lauryl sulphate and \ndilute to 1000 ml with wu/er, m\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 45 minutes. ''’2;. a < \n- .\nWithdrawn suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) .\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolutionmedium.\nReference solution. A 0.025 per cent w/v solution of \ndutasteride 1PRS in mobile phase. Dilute 2.0 ml of the solution \nto 5,00.0 ml with dissolution medium.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- .mobile.phase: a mixture of 40,0 volumes of a buffer\nsolution prepared by 0.05 M sodium dihydrogen \nphosphate monohydrate arid adjusted to pH 5.0 with \n,. dilute sodium hydroxide and 60 volumes of acetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1ml per minute, \n,\n.. . \nspectrophotometer set at 240 nm, s p.,\n- injection volume: 200 pl. .. \n, , \n.\nInj