 test solution; disregard any \npeak due to mesityl oxide;\nSo = sum of the areas of the peaks with a relative\nretention more than 1.25;\nS\\ = sum of the areas of the peaks due to\nteicoplauin A2.] group in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution;\nS2 “ area of the peak due to teicoplauin A2-2 in the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution;\nS3 = sum of the areas of the peaks, due to\n, teicoplauin A2.3 group in the chromatogram\nobtained with the lest solution; . . ..\nS4 = area of the peak due to teicoplauin A2.4 in the\nchromatogramobtained with the test solution;\n> S5 ~ sum of the areas of the peaks due to\nteicoplauin A2.5 group in the,.chromatogram \nobtained with. the.test solution. \n. :\nThe area of any secondary peak corresponding to teicoplanin \nA2 group is not less than 80.0!per cent; teicoplanin A2.2 group \nis not less than 35.0per cent and not more than55.0 per cent. \nTeicoplanin A2_) group is not more than 20.0 per cent, \nteicoplanin teicoplanin A2.3 group is not more than 20.0 per \ncent, teicoplanin A2.4 group is not more.than 20.0 per cent, \nteicoplanin teicoplanin A2.,5 group is not more than 20.0 per \ncent and teicoplanin A3 group is not more than:15.0.per cent \nand the sum of the areas of all other secondary peak other \nthan mesityl oxide with a relative retention time 1.25 times is \nnot more than 5.0 percent. Ignore the peak due to: teicoplanin \nA2.2 with an area less'than0 j5 times ofthe principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (0.25 per \ncent). ; \n‘\nImpurity A. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nUse the Chromatographic system as described under test for \nComposition and related substances. ' \n;\nName \n.. \nRelative\nAd •- •.............'___________________retention time\nTeicoplann impurity A1 \n0.6\nTeicoplann A2.2 (Retention time: about 18 minutes) 1.0\n'4-methylpent-3-en-2-one (mesityl oxide).\nInject reference solution (c)!and the test solution. The area bf \n