contains riot less:ihah \n90.0 per cent and not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated \namount of telmisartan, \namlodipii^\nQoH^ClNoQ,\nUsual strengths. Telmisartan, 40 mg and amlodipine, 5 mg; \nTelmisartan, 80 mg and amlodipine, 10 mg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Iri the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to. the:peak..in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (e). L-\nTests .\nDissolution (2.5.2). \n1\nFor Amlodipine —\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), \n■ \nMedium. 500 ml 0.01 Mhydrdchloric acid, \" '! '\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the mediurh arid filter.\nSpeed and time.75rpm and 20 minutes.\nDetermine^ by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). i ;\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium.. / \n; \n; \n/;■;\nReference solution.!^ 0.001 per cent w/v solution of amlpdipiffl\nbesylate IPRS in the dissolution medium. \n,\nChromatographic system\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), \n- sample temperature: 10°, r \n.... \n- \nmobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of a buffer solutioh \nprepared;by, dissolving 3.43 g monobasic sodiuif\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\n' ;. phosphate dihydrate and 2 ml of triethylpmine io\n1000 ml of water and adjusted to pH 6.0 with \northophosphoric acid and 40 volumes of acetonitrile,^ \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, ' \n\\\nIH^O22\n_? spectrophotometer set at 257 rim, \n^injççtiopvolume: 20 pl.\nreference solution. The test is not valid unless the \nfactor is not more than 2.5 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C20H2SCIN2O5.\nq Not less than 80 per cent of thé stated amount of \n¿h¿cin2o5. J -■■■■'■ '\n■V;? ‘ïiom u. ■ v ■'■■■■'■: ■■■\nFofTelmisartan ' \n......\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), \n,\nMedium 900 ml of phosphate buffer pH 7.5,. prepared by \ndissolving 6.8 g of monobasic potassium phosphate and\n1.52gi<W/ww hydroxide in 1000 mlof water, adjusted to pH \n75 vrith dilute sodium hydroxide,\nSpeed and time. 7 5 rpm and 20 minutes. \n. \n, \n.\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. Add 5 volumes of triethylamine in 500 \nvolumes of water and further add 500 volumes of acetonitrile \nandmix.\nTestfaluHon. Usé the” filtrate,' dilute 'if necessary, with thé\ndissolution medium. \n.\nFffprencpsplutipn'. A0.1 per centw/v solution of telmisartan \nWSinsol ven t mixture. Dilute 5.0 ml of the solution to 1Q0.0 \nmlwiththç dissolution medium.\nUse chromatographic system as described under dissolution \nofAmlodipine. \n'\nInject:the’¿reference sblutiomThe test is not valid unless the \ntailirigfactor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C33H30N4O2.\nQ. Not less than 80 per cent of the. stated amount of \nC3iH30N4O2.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14),\nSolvent mixture. 10 volumes of 0. IM hydrochloric acid and \n90 volumes of methanol.\nTe&solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets into fine powder. \nTransfer the powder containing 25 mg of Amlodipine into\n100.0 mJ volumetric flask and dissolve in about 70.0 ml solvent\nH^xture and sonicate for 45 minutes. After sonication bring\nsolution into room temperature and dilute to volume up to\n^hemark with solvent mixture. \n■\nTELMISARTAN AND AMLODIPINE TABLETS\nReference solution, (a).A 0.004 per cent .w/v solution of \ntelmisartan IP RS in solvent mixture.; \n. >■\nReference solution (b)j\\ solution of amlodipine besylate IPRS\ncontaining 0.00125 per cent w/v of amlodipine in solvent \nmixture. ’ ’ \n' \n- \n■■ ■\nReference solution (c). Transfer 5ml of reference solution\n(a) and 2 ml of reference solution (b) in 100.0 ml volumetirc \nflask and dilute to volume upto the mark with solvent \nmixture and mix. \n. \n;\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- mobile phase: A. a mixture of 85 volumes of a buffer\nsolution prepared by dissolving 1.36 g potassium \ndihydrogen orthophosphate inlOOO.O.ml of waterand \nadjusted to pH 3.2 with orthophosphoric acid and\n15 volumes of acetonitrile.\nB. a mixture of 15 volumes of a buffer \nsolution prepared by dissolving 1.36 g potassium \ndihydrogen orthophosphate in 1000.0 ml of water arid\n' adjusted to pH 3.2 .with orthophosphoric acid and\n85 volumes of acetonitrile. \n; '\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n- flowrate: 1.5 ml per minute, !\n- spectrophotometer set at 237 nm,\ninjection volume: 25 pl..\nTime .\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n' 85\n■ ' 7 15\n7\n' \n85 ■’■■■■ ■\n15\n■■ 15\n...... \", 90 \n■ •\n10\n' 20\n75\n25\n■ 35 ■\n60\n40\n40\n■ 55 •\n■ 45\n■45\n45\n55\n’ 50\n35\n65\n55\n85\n. J 15 .\n60\n85\n15\nInject reference solution (c). The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency for both the peak is not less than 1500 \ntheoretical plates, the tailing factor is not more than 2.0 and \nthe relative standard deviation for replicate injections is not \nmore than 5.0 per cent.\nThe relative retention time with reference to amlodipine for \nImpurity D (3-ethyl 5-methyl 2-[(2-aminoethoxy)methyl]-4-(2- \nchlorophenyl)-6-methylpyridine-3,5-dicarboxylate) is 0.5. \nMultiply the peak area of impurity D by correction factor 2.58.\nInject reference solution (c) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any\npeak due to impurity D of amlodipine is not more than the\n10 times the area of the amlodipine principal peak in reference \nsolution (c) (1.0 per cent). The area of. any secondary peak \ndue to amlodipine, and telmisartan is not more than foe 5, times \nthe area of the telmisartan principal peak in reference solution \n(c), (0,5 per cent) and the sum of the areas of the all secondary \npeaks excluding Impurity D is hot more than 20 times the area \nof the principal peak of telmisartan in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (c) (2.0 per cent)..lgnore any \npeaks with an area less than 0.5 times of telmisartan peak in \nchromatogram obtained with referen"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/telmisartan-and-hydrochlorothiazide-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Telmisartan and Hydrochlorothiazide Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Telmisartan and Hydrochlorothiazide \nTablets \n.....\nTelmisartan and Hydrochlorothiazide Tablets contain not less \nthan 95.0 per cent arid not more than ’105:0 per'cent :oï the \nstated amount of telmisartan C33HMN4O?. and riot less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 107.5 per cent of the stated \namount of hydrochlorothiazide C7H8C1N3O4S2. \niv\nUsual strengths., Telmisartan^ 40 mg and Hydrochlorothiazide,\n12.5 mg; Telmisartan, 80 mg and Hydrochlorothiazide;! 2.5 mg-\n‘ \n: \\ : \n1 '.•<)'? •• p Of; ii d"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Telmisartan and Hydrochlorothiazide \nTablets \n.....\nTelmisartan and Hydrochlorothiazide Tablets contain not less \nthan 95.0 per cent arid not more than ’105:0 per'cent :oï the \nstated amount of telmisartan C33HMN4O?. and riot less than \n90.0 per cent and not more than 107.5 per cent of the stated \namount of hydrochlorothiazide C7H8C1N3O4S2. \niv\nUsual strengths., Telmisartan^ 40 mg and Hydrochlorothiazide,\n12.5 mg; Telmisartan, 80 mg and Hydrochlorothiazide;! 2.5 mg-\n‘ \n: \\ : \n1 '.•<)'? •• p Of; ii d"},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the principal peaks in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peaks in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c)J ; ■ ’ '' )\nTests . .\nDissolution (2.5.2). \n! 1 7\nFor Telmisartan— • \n• \n• \n--\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), \n-v.\nMedium. 900 ml of a phosphate buffer pH 7.5, prepared by \ndissolving 13.61 g of potassium dihydrogen phosphate^\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 30 minutes. . \n. ,. r'i’\n1000 ml of water, adjusted to pH 7.5 with 2 Msodium hydrops\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the inedium and filter/'5\n^^drochlorothiazide— \n^SiátusNo. 1 (Basket),\n:. 900 ml of 0.1 M hydrochloric acid,\nSpeed and time. 100 rpm and 30 minutes.\n^itítdráw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\n^¿rmine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\ns\"r:' ’■¡^7Í ’\nTest solution. Use the filtrate, dilute if necessary, with the \ndissolutionmedium.\nReference solution (a). Dissolve a quantity of telmisartan \n^S in minimum quantity of methanol and dilute with \ndissolution medium to obtain a solution having a known \nconcentration similar to the test solution. .\nijp^ence solution (b). Dissolve a quantity of\nhydrochlorthiazide IPRS in minimum quantity of methanol \nand dilutewith dissolution medium to obtain a solution having \naknown concentration similar to the test solution.\n^¡iihmaiographic system\n. - a stainless steel column 6 cm x 3.0 mm, packed with\n; ú u ■QQtylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- column temperature: 40°,\n- mobile phase: A. a buffer solution prepared by\ndissolving 5.0 g of ammonium dihydrogen ortho­\nphosphate in 1000 ml of water, adjusted to pH 3.0 with\ndiluted phosphoroic acid,\n■ <-• \nB. acetonitrile,\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\nspectrophotometer set at 270 nm for hydrochlorothiazide \nand 298 nm for telmisartan,\n- injection volume: 4 pl.\nTime\nMobile\nMobile\nFlow rate\nphase A\nphase B\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n(ml per min.)\no '\n85\n15\n0.6\n(in min.)\n\"• 1.5\n85\n15\n0.6\ni? 151\n60\n40\n0.6\n5.0\n' 60\n40\n0.6\n5.01\n20\n80\n1.0\n6.2\n20\n80\n1-0\n621\n85\n15\n0.6\n; 9.7\n85\n15\n0.6\nThe relative retention time with reference to telmisartan for \nhydrochlorothiazide is about 0.33.\nInject reference solution (a) and (b). The test is not valid unless \nthe tailing factor for each peak is not more than 2.5 and the \nrelative standard deviation for replicate injections for each \nPeak is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nTELMISARTAN AND HYDROCHLOROTHIAZIDE TABLETS\nInject reference solution (a) and (b) and the test solution.\nQ. Not less than 80 per cent of the stated amount of \nandC7H8ClN3O4S2.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14), as described under Assay with the following \nmodifications.\nReference solution (d). A 0.0025 per cent w/v solution of \n4-Amino-6-chloro-1,3-benzenedisulphonamide IPRS \n(benzothiadiqzine impurity A IPRS) in the solvent mixture \nand further dilute with a solution prepared by diluting equal \nvolumes of mobile phase A and mobile phase B to obtain a \nfinal concentration: of; 0.00005 per cent w/v for telmisartan \n40 mg and hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg and 0.000025 per cent \nw/vfor.telmisartan 80 mg and hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg.\nReference solution (e). A solution containing0.016 per cent \nw/v of telmisartan IPRS and 0.005 per cent w/v \nhydrochlorothiazide IPRS in the solvent mixture. Dilute\n1.0 ml of the solution and 2.0 ml of0.0025 per cent w/v solution \nof benzothiadiazine impurity A RS in the solvent mixture to\n100.0 ml with the solvent mixture and further dilute 1.0 ml of \nthe solution to 5.0 ml with a solution prepared by diluting \nequal volumes of mobile phase A and mobile phase B.\nInject reference solution (c) and (e). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to hydrochlorothiazide \nand benzothiadiazine impurity A in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (c) is not less than 2.0 and the relative \nstandard deviation for replicate injections for both peaks of \ntelmisartan and hydrochlorothiazide in thechromatdgram \nobtained with reference'solution (c) is not more than 2.0 per \ncent. The signal to noise ratio for the telmisartan, \nhydrochlorothiazide and benzothiadiazine impurity A peaks \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (e) is \nnot less than 3.0.\nInject reference solution (c), (d) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \npeak corresponding to benzothiadiazine impurity Ais not more \nthan 6.4 times the area of the benzothiadiazine impurity A \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(d) (1.0 per cent),the area of any individual secondary peak \ndue to telmisartan is not more than 0.005 times the area of the \ntelmisartan peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (c) (0.5 per cent), the area of any individual secondary \npeak due to hydrochlorothiazide is not more than 0.002 times \nthe area of the hydrochlorothiazide peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (c) (0.2 per cent) and the sum \nof areas of all the secondary peaks due to telmisartan is not \nmore than 0.005 times the area of the telmisartan peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) (0.5 per \ncent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks due to \nhydrochlorothiazide is not more than 0.02 times the area of the\nhydrochlorothiazide peak in thechromatogram obiained with \nreference solution (c) (2.0 per cent).\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated underTabletsï m\nAssay: Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14)2 - ? h> ?.\nSolvent mixture, 0,005 M methanolic solution of sodium \nhydroxide.\nNOTE ;— To prevent heat from degrading the sample, do not\nextend the sonication time and also maintain the bath \ntemperature at a temperature not exceeding 22° by adding \nice, . \n, ■ \n. ; ' . ’ ; ;..L '. rr„; . \n. ...\nTest solution. Weigh and disperse 10 intact tablets in a suitable \nvolumetric flask, add 0.T ;M Sodium hydroxide solution; not \nexceeding 5 per cent of the total volume "}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/telmisartan-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Telmisartan Tablets","la":"Identification"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TELMISARTAN TABLETS"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TELMISARTAN TABLETS"},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle),\nMedium. 900 ml of phosphate buffer pH 7.5, prepared by \ndissolving 13.61 g of potassium dihydrogen phosphate in \nabout 800 ml of water, adjusted to pH 7.5 with 2M sodium \nhydroxide, and diluted with water to 1000 ml, ;\nSpeed and time. 75 rpm for 30 minutes.\nWithdraw a suitable voltime of the medium and filter. Reject \nthe first few ml of the filtrate and dilute a suitable volume of\nthe filtrate with dissolution medium. Measure the absorbance \nof the resulting solution at the maximum at about296 nm (2.4.7). \nCalculate the content of C33H30N4O2 in the medium from the \nabsorbance obtained from a solution prepared by dissolving \n44 mg of teimisartan IPRS in 1 ml of 0. IM sodium hydroxide, \nand dilute to 100 ml with methanol. Further dilute the solution \nwith dissolution medium to obtain a solution with a final \nconcentration of 0.0011 per cent of teimisartan.\nQ. Not. less, than 75 per cent of the stated amount of\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 80 volumes of buffer solution prepared by \ndiluting 5.0 ml Of triethylamine to 2000 ml with water and 20 \nvolumes of methanol.\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof powder containing 100 mg of Teimisartan in 100:0 ml of \nsolvent mixture with the aid of ultrasound for 45 minutes and \nfilter.\nReference solution. A 0.0005 per cent w/v solution of\nteimisartan IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5-pm) (Such \nas Inertsil ODS-3), \n. <\n- mobile phase: A. dissolve 0.5 g of potassium\ndihydrogen phosphate in 1000 ml of water, add 2 ml of \ntriethylamine, adjusted to pH 3 ;2 with orthophosphoric\n.. acid, • • J '<'</■■\nB: acetonitrile,\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 1.8 ml per minute;\n- spectrophotometer set at 298 nm,\n- injectionvolume:20pl.\nTime\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(in min.)\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n■ 6 . ■,\n80. ■ . ,\n.• -/ \n20 \n.\n7.\n70\n30\n15\n60\n40\n25 .\n60\n40\n26\n40\n60\n35. .\n'■ ’ï æ '\n^40\n.78'.\n22 \n> .\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntheoretical plates is not less than 3000, tailing' factor is not \nmore than 2.0 and relative standard; deviation for. replicate\ninjections is not morc than 5.0 per cent. \n- .\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(0.5 per cent), the sum of the areas of all the secondary peaks \nis hot more than 4 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (2.0 per cent). \nIgnore any peak with atiaf ea less than 0.1 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference \nsolution(0.05 percent). \n:-\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets;\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture, 80 volumes of buffer solution prepared by \ndiluting 5.0 ml of triethylamine to 2000 ml with water, and 20 \nvolumes of methanol.\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof powder containing 40 mg of Telmisartan in 100 ml of the \nsolvent mixture and sonicate for 45 minutes. Dilute 5.0 ml of \nthe solution to 50.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution..A; Q.004 per cent w/v solution of \ntelmisartan IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system\n- \n¡a stainless;steel.column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm) (such \nas Inertsil ODS-3), \n; \n. . , ; \\ \n: <\n; . \nmobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of buffer solution\nprepared by dissolving 2.72 g-ofpotassium dihydrogen \nphosphate in 1000 ml of water, add 2 ml of triethylamine\nand adjusted to pH 2.4 with orthophosphoric acid and \n40 volumes of acetonitrile, : ।. b.c':\n- flow rale: 1 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 298. nm, \n- < . ; ; . ,\n- injection volume: 20 pl. \n•\nTELMISARTAN '■ TABLETS\nIp 2022\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid Unless the ' \ntheoretical plates is not less than 3000, the tailing factor is not \nmore than 2:0 and thé relative standard deviation forri$plica(e \ninjections is not more than 2.0 per cent. \n- ;\nInject the reference solution arid thé test solution. ’ \n‘\nCalculate the content of C ;3HWN4O2 in the tablets. ' \n'' '' '\nA ; \n; \n...¡AT"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/telmisartan","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Telmisartan"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TELMISARTAN '\nThe area of peaks corresponding to teicoplanin A2 group is \nnot less than 75.0 per cent, teicoplanin A3 group is not more \nthan 20.0 per cent and the sum of the areas of all other \nsecondary peaks with a relative retention time more than 1.25 \nis hot more than 5.0 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 5.0 per cent, determined on \no.5g. ■ \n’\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2.3). Not more than 0.30 Endotoxin \nunit per mg of teicoplanin.\nSterility (2.2.11). Complies with the test for sterility.\nAssay. Determine by the microbiological assay of antibiotics, \nMethod A (2.2.10) on a solution prepared in the following \nmanner. \n■ . ..-T-v..;' \n■ \n;■\nReconstitute teicoplanin for injection as directed in the labeling. \nWithdraw an accurately measured volume of a resultant \nsolution, using; a suitable hypodermic needle and syringe, \nand dilute, quantitatively and stepwise with buffer.\nThe upper fiducial limit of error is not less than 90.0 per cent \nand the lower fiducial limit of errors is not more than 120 per \ncent of the estimated potency.\nStorage. Store in a cool place.\nTelmisartan *\n■............ ■ ■■ ............. ' .■\nC33H3oN402 \n' \nMol. Wt. 514.6\nTelmisartan is 4'- {[4-methyl-6-( 1 -methyl-1 ZAbenzimidazo 1-2- \nyl)-2 -propyl-1 //-benzimi dazo 1 - J -y 1 ] methyl} -2 -b ip heny I - \ncarboxylic acid.\nTelmisartan contains not less than 98.0 per cent and not more \nthan 102.0 per cent of \ncalculated on the dried\nbasis. ' : \n\"7/\nCategory. Antihypertensive.\nDescription. A white to off-white crystalline powder.\nIP 2022 B"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TELMISARTAN '\nThe area of peaks corresponding to teicoplanin A2 group is \nnot less than 75.0 per cent, teicoplanin A3 group is not more \nthan 20.0 per cent and the sum of the areas of all other \nsecondary peaks with a relative retention time more than 1.25 \nis hot more than 5.0 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 5.0 per cent, determined on \no.5g. ■ \n’\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2.3). Not more than 0.30 Endotoxin \nunit per mg of teicoplanin.\nSterility (2.2.11). Complies with the test for sterility.\nAssay. Determine by the microbiological assay of antibiotics, \nMethod A (2.2.10) on a solution prepared in the following \nmanner. \n■ . ..-T-v..;' \n■ \n;■\nReconstitute teicoplanin for injection as directed in the labeling. \nWithdraw an accurately measured volume of a resultant \nsolution, using; a suitable hypodermic needle and syringe, \nand dilute, quantitatively and stepwise with buffer.\nThe upper fiducial limit of error is not less than 90.0 per cent \nand the lower fiducial limit of errors is not more than 120 per \ncent of the estimated potency.\nStorage. Store in a cool place.\nTelmisartan *\n■............ ■ ■■ ............. ' .■\nC33H3oN402 \n' \nMol. Wt. 514.6\nTelmisartan is 4'- {[4-methyl-6-( 1 -methyl-1 ZAbenzimidazo 1-2- \nyl)-2 -propyl-1 //-benzimi dazo 1 - J -y 1 ] methyl} -2 -b ip heny I - \ncarboxylic acid.\nTelmisartan contains not less than 98.0 per cent and not more \nthan 102.0 per cent of \ncalculated on the dried\nbasis. ' : \n\"7/\nCategory. Antihypertensive.\nDescription. A white to off-white crystalline powder.\nIP 2022 B"},{"name":"Identification","text":"f\nDetermine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6) B \nCompare: the spectrum with that obtained with telmisartan \nIPRS or with the reference spectrum of telmisartan. ; |"},{"name":"Tests","text":"';ir' \n': -T 3\nAppearance of solution. A 5 per cent w/v solution in 1 y \nsodium hydroxide is not more intensely coloured than \nreference solution YS4 (2.4.1). \n. , ; , : . ( ••\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \n’ ■'* V\nTest solution. Dissolve about 25 mg of the substance under \nexamination in 5 ml of methanol, add 100 pl of a 4 per cent w/v \nsolution of sodium hydroxide and dilute to. 50.0 ml with \nmethanol.\nReference solution- Dilute 1.0 ml ofthe test solution to 10.0 ml \nwith methanol. Dilute 1.0 ml of the solutionto 1 QO.O ml with \nmethanol. \n■\nChromatographicsystem \n;\n■ a stainless steel column 12.5 cm x 4.0 mm, packcdwith\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), (Such \nas Thermoquest),\n- column temperature: 40°,\n- mobile phase: A. dissolve 2.0 g ofpotassium dihydrogen\nphosphate and 3.8 g of sodium pentanesulphonate\nmonohydrate in water, adjusted to pH 3.0 with \northophosphoric acid and dilute to 1000ml with wafer,\nB. a mixture of 20 volumes of methanol \nand 80 volumes of acetonitrile, \n- .\n- a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 230 nm,\n- injection volume: 10 pl.\nTime Mobile phase A \n(in mip.) . (per cent v/y)\nMobile phase B\n(per cent v/y)\n30 :\n0 \n70 . \n.\n3 \n.70.\n28 \n20\n30 / \n70\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntheoretical plates is not less than 2000, tailing factor is not \nmore than 2.0 and the relative standard deviation for replicate \ninjections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the ,area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than twice the area of the principal \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(0.2 per cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondarypeaks\n- ot&Q& ^an ^mcs tire area of the principal peak in the\ni.fOiriatogram obtained with the reference solution (1.0 per \n„pnty lgnore any peak with an area less than 0.5 times the .area\nf^e.principal peak in the. chromatogram obtained with the\nreference solution (0.05 per cent)."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Heavy metals (2.3.13). 1.0 g complies with the limit test for \nheavy metals, Method B (20 ppm).\ngulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\n£os$ on drying (2.4.19). Not more than 0.5 per cent, determined \non 1 gby drying in oven at 105°. \n■ \n: '\nAssay.:Determine by liquicl chrornatography(2.4.14). .. . .\nSolvent mixture. 80 volumes of buffer solution prepared by \n¿luting 5.0 ml of triethylamine to 2000 ml with water and 20 \nvolumes of methanol.\nTesi solution. Dissolve 40 mg of substance under examination \nini 00.0 ml of the solvent mixture. Dilute 5.0 ml of the solution \nto 50;0 ml with the solvent .mixture.\nReference solution. A 0.004 per cent w/v solution of \nteimisartan IPRS in the solvent mixture.\nChromatographic system\n; . a stainless steel column 15cmx 4.6 mm, packed with \nmi : octadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm) (such\nas Inertsil ODS-3),\nC33H30N4O2.\n■ mobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of buffer solution \n\\ , prepared by dissolving 2.72 g ofpotassium dihydrogen\nphosphate in 1000 ml of water, add 2 ml ofirielhylamine\nand adjusted to pH 2.4 with orthophosphoric acid and\n40 volumes of acetonitrile,\n~~ flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 298 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 ul. .\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntheoretical plates is not less than 3000, the tailing factor is not \nmore than 2.0 and the relative standard deviation for replicate \ninjections is not more than 2.0 per. cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C33H30N4O2.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nTeimisartan Tablets\nTeimisartan Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and \nhot more than 1 ¡0.0 per cent of the stated amount of \nteimisartan, C33H30N4O2.\nvisual strengths. 20 mg; 40 mg; 80 mg.."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/temozolomide-capsules","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Temozolomide Capsules","la":"Identification"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TEMOZOLOMIDE CAPSULES\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. Run. the \nchromatogram 3.2 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. The area of any péàk due to 2-azahypoxanthine is not \nmore than twice the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (à) (0.2 per \ncent), the area of any peak due to temozolomide related \ncompound A is not more than 5 times the area of principal \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding to \ntemozolomide acid and aminoimidazolecârboxàmidë, each of, \nis not more than the area of the principal peak, in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solutipn.(a),(0.1 per \ncent), the area of any peak corresponding to cyanptemozol \nomide is not more than 1.5 times the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.15 \nper cent), the area of any other secondary peak is hot more \nthan the area of the principal peak;in. the = chromatogram\nobtained with reference solution (a) (0.1 pencent) and the \nsum of the areas . of all the secondary peaks is not more than 8 \ntimes the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (a) (0.8 per cent)..\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). 0.67 g complies with the limit test for \nheavy metals, Method B (30 ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 0.4 per cent, using method 3.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as\ndescribed under Related substances using following \nmodifications.\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution of \ntemozolomidè IPRS in dimethylsulphoxide.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 1.9 and the relative standard \ndeviation of replicate injections is not more than 1.5.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C6H6N6O2.\nStorage. Store protectedfrom light and moisture.\nTemozolomide Capsules\nTemozolomide Capsules/contain not less Than 90.0 per cent \nand not more than 110.0 per cent bf the stated amount of \ntemozolomide, C6H6N6O2.\nCAUTION—Temozolomide iscytotoxic; extra care required \nto prevent inhaling particles and exposing the skin to it.\nUsual strengths. 20 mg; 100 mg; 250 mg. \n< :\nTEMOZOLOMIDE CAPSULES"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TEMOZOLOMIDE CAPSULES\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. Run. the \nchromatogram 3.2 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. The area of any péàk due to 2-azahypoxanthine is not \nmore than twice the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (à) (0.2 per \ncent), the area of any peak due to temozolomide related \ncompound A is not more than 5 times the area of principal \npeak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding to \ntemozolomide acid and aminoimidazolecârboxàmidë, each of, \nis not more than the area of the principal peak, in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solutipn.(a),(0.1 per \ncent), the area of any peak corresponding to cyanptemozol \nomide is not more than 1.5 times the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.15 \nper cent), the area of any other secondary peak is hot more \nthan the area of the principal peak;in. the = chromatogram\nobtained with reference solution (a) (0.1 pencent) and the \nsum of the areas . of all the secondary peaks is not more than 8 \ntimes the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (a) (0.8 per cent)..\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). 0.67 g complies with the limit test for \nheavy metals, Method B (30 ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 0.4 per cent, using method 3.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as\ndescribed under Related substances using following \nmodifications.\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution of \ntemozolomidè IPRS in dimethylsulphoxide.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 1.9 and the relative standard \ndeviation of replicate injections is not more than 1.5.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C6H6N6O2.\nStorage. Store protectedfrom light and moisture.\nTemozolomide Capsules\nTemozolomide Capsules/contain not less Than 90.0 per cent \nand not more than 110.0 per cent bf the stated amount of \ntemozolomide, C6H6N6O2.\nCAUTION—Temozolomide iscytotoxic; extra care required \nto prevent inhaling particles and exposing the skin to it.\nUsual strengths. 20 mg; 100 mg; 250 mg. \n< :\nTEMOZOLOMIDE CAPSULES"},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, .the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test, solution corresponds to. the, peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution.\nTests ,, .. \n. \n.?\nOther tests. Comply with tests stated under capsules.\nAssay. Determine by liquid; chromatography (2.4.14).- ,\nTest solution.: Weigh a quantity of mixed contents of 20 \ncapsules containing 20 mg of Temozolomide in 100.0 mI of \nmobilephàse. \n-- ’ d \n■-1\nReference solution. A 0,02 per cent w/v solution of\ntemozolomide IPRS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system ; \n, - ■ ; \nn\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5' pm) (Such \nas Hypersil BDS), ; ■ ’ < : \n,\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 90 volumes of 0.5 per cent\n, v/v acetic acid and 10 ml volumes of acetonitrile,\n■ flowrate: 1 mlperminute, \n'\n- spectrophotometer set at 329 nm,\n- \ninjection volume: 20 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The; test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0, the column efficiency is not \nless than 2000 theoretical plates and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is hot more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C6H6N6O2 in the capsules.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/temozolomide-impurity-a2","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Temozolomide impurity A2"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Temozolomide impurity A2\n0.53\nTemozolomide acid3 \t\n0.84\nTemozolomide \t\n1.0\nDacarbazine impurity A4\n1.37 \n(free base)\n'4a.5-dihydro-4H -imidazo[4.5-d][1,2.3]triazin-4-one,\n24-diazo-4H -imidazole-5-carboxamide,\n33-methyl-4-oxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5,1-d][1,2,3,5]tetrazine -8-\n carboxylic acid,\n45-aminoimidazole-4-carboxamide. It is a free base of dacarbazine \nimpurityA\nInject the reference solution.The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to temozolomide and \ndacarbazine impurity A is not less than 2.0.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 3.2 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. In the chromatogram obtained with the test solution, \nthe area of any peak due to 2-azahypoxanthine is not more \nthan the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the reference solution (0.2 per cent), the area of \nany peak due to temozolomide impurityA is not more than 2.5 \ntimes the area of principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the reference solution (0.5 per cent), the area of the any \npeak due temozolomide acid is not more than 0.5 times the \narea of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nthe reference solution (0.1 per cent), the area of peak due to \ndacarbazine impurity A is not more than 0.5 times the area of \nthe principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with the \nreference solution (0.1 per cent) and the area of any other \nsecondary peak is not more than 0.5 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference \nsolution (0.1 per cent). The sum of the areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 4 times the area of the principal peak in \nthe chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(0.8 per cent).\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). 0.67 g complies with the limit test for \nheavy metals, Method B (30 ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 0.4 per cent, using method 3. \nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as \ndescribed in the Related substances using following \nmodifications. \nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent wiv.  \ntemozolomide RS in dimethylsulphoxide."},"sections":[{"name":"CONTENT","text":"Temozolomide impurity A2\n0.53\nTemozolomide acid3 \t\n0.84\nTemozolomide \t\n1.0\nDacarbazine impurity A4\n1.37 \n(free base)\n'4a.5-dihydro-4H -imidazo[4.5-d][1,2.3]triazin-4-one,\n24-diazo-4H -imidazole-5-carboxamide,\n33-methyl-4-oxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5,1-d][1,2,3,5]tetrazine -8-\n carboxylic acid,\n45-aminoimidazole-4-carboxamide. It is a free base of dacarbazine \nimpurityA\nInject the reference solution.The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to temozolomide and \ndacarbazine impurity A is not less than 2.0.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 3.2 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. In the chromatogram obtained with the test solution, \nthe area of any peak due to 2-azahypoxanthine is not more \nthan the area of the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the reference solution (0.2 per cent), the area of \nany peak due to temozolomide impurityA is not more than 2.5 \ntimes the area of principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the reference solution (0.5 per cent), the area of the any \npeak due temozolomide acid is not more than 0.5 times the \narea of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nthe reference solution (0.1 per cent), the area of peak due to \ndacarbazine impurity A is not more than 0.5 times the area of \nthe principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with the \nreference solution (0.1 per cent) and the area of any other \nsecondary peak is not more than 0.5 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with the reference \nsolution (0.1 per cent). The sum of the areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than 4 times the area of the principal peak in \nthe chromatogram obtained with the reference solution \n(0.8 per cent).\nHeavy metals (2.3.13). 0.67 g complies with the limit test for \nheavy metals, Method B (30 ppm).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.1 per cent.\nWater (2.3.43). Not more than 0.4 per cent, using method 3. \nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as \ndescribed in the Related substances using following \nmodifications. \nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent wiv.  \ntemozolomide RS in dimethylsulphoxide."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/temozolomide-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Temozolomide Injection"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Temozolomide Injection\nTemozolomide Injection is a sterile, lyophilized material \nconsisting of Temozolomide with of without excipients. It is \nfilled in a sealed container.\nTemozolomide Injection contains not less than 95.0 per cent \nand not more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntemozolomide,C6H()N6O2. -■ ? \n■\nNOTE — Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing thé 'skin to it.\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of:solution, and Particulate matter stated, under \nParenteral Preparations. (Injections). .\nUsual strength. 100 mg. \n. ; P \n, b\nStorage^ The reconstituted solution stand atroomtempei \nmust be used within 14 frours, including infusion time.\nThe content of the sealed container comply with the \nrequirements stated under Parenteral Preparation (Poyfo \nfor Injection) and with the following requirement. ' ' 'x"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Temozolomide Injection\nTemozolomide Injection is a sterile, lyophilized material \nconsisting of Temozolomide with of without excipients. It is \nfilled in a sealed container.\nTemozolomide Injection contains not less than 95.0 per cent \nand not more than 105.0 per cent of the stated amount of \ntemozolomide,C6H()N6O2. -■ ? \n■\nNOTE — Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing thé 'skin to it.\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of:solution, and Particulate matter stated, under \nParenteral Preparations. (Injections). .\nUsual strength. 100 mg. \n. ; P \n, b\nStorage^ The reconstituted solution stand atroomtempei \nmust be used within 14 frours, including infusion time.\nThe content of the sealed container comply with the \nrequirements stated under Parenteral Preparation (Poyfo \nfor Injection) and with the following requirement. ' ' 'x"},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Disperse a quantity óf injection containing 50 mg of \ntemozolomide methylene chloride with the aid of ultrasound \nfor 30 minutes and filter.Evaporate the filtrate under a stream \nof nitrogen to dryness. On.the residue, determine by. infrared \nabsorption spectrophotometry.(2.4.6). Compare the spectrum \nwith that obtained with temozolomide IPRS treated in similar \nmanner or with the reference spectrum of temozolomide.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the .peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a)."},{"name":"Tests","text":"pH (2.4.28). 3.0 to 4.5, determined on a freshly constituted vial \nof temozolomide injection, using 40 ml carbon-.dioxide free \nwater. \n;. w \n■■■• ■>' -■ \n■ :\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). \n; \n■’ L z ' 'y ■\nTest solution. Reconstitute 5 vials with each of 40 ml of wafer, \nwith the aid of ultrasound, combine and dilute to 250.0 ml with \nwater. Dilute 5.0 ml of the solution to ,100.0 ml with the mobile \nphase. \n.............\nReference solution (a).-. A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of \ntemozolomide IPRS in the mobile phase. . \n:,..... \n.\nReference solution (b). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution (a) \nto 100.0 ml with the mobile phase. \n■-\nReference solution (c): Transfer 50 ml of 0.1 M hydrochloric \nacid and 50 ml of reference solution (a) to a suitable glass \ncontainer. Heat the container at 80° for 4 hours. Dilute, 10.0 ml \nof the solution to 25.0 ml with the mobile phase. (NOTE—the \npreparation forms 2-azahypoxanthine, temozolomide acid\nand aminoimidazole carboxamide). \n: .\nReference solution (d). Diluted .0 ml of reference solution (b) \nto 10.0 ml with the mobile phase. ’ '\nChromatographic system :\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm * 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), :\n. - sample temperature: 2° to 8°,\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 96 volumes of 0.5 per cent\nv/v solution of glacial acetic acid in .watered \n4 volumes of zwe/Zîa/zoZ containing 0.094 per cent w/vof\nsodium 1-hexanesulphonate, ■■■■'. ‘"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/temozolomide","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Temozolomide"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Temozolomide\no\nC;,H6N6O2 \nMol. Wt 194.2\nTemozolomide is 3,4-dihydro-3-mcthyl-4-oxoimidazo[5,l-i/]-\n1,2,3,5-tetrazine-8-carboxamide.\nTemozolomide contains not less than 98.0 per centand not \nmore than 102.0 per cent of C6H6N6O2, calculated on anhydrous \nbasis. \n!\nCategory. Anticancer.\nDescription. A white to light pink or light tan powder.\nNOTE— Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing the skin to it. y"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Temozolomide\no\nC;,H6N6O2 \nMol. Wt 194.2\nTemozolomide is 3,4-dihydro-3-mcthyl-4-oxoimidazo[5,l-i/]-\n1,2,3,5-tetrazine-8-carboxamide.\nTemozolomide contains not less than 98.0 per centand not \nmore than 102.0 per cent of C6H6N6O2, calculated on anhydrous \nbasis. \n!\nCategory. Anticancer.\nDescription. A white to light pink or light tan powder.\nNOTE— Temozolomide is cytotoxic; extra care required to \nprevent inhaling particles and exposing the skin to it. y"},{"name":"Identification","text":";\nAi Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotomctry(2.4.6). \nCompare the. spectrum with that obtained with temozolomide \nIPRS or with the reference spectrum of temozolomide, /soy\nft lnithp;AssaV’ the PrinciPal Peak m thc c}iromatogram \n^¿j;with the test solution corresponds to the peak 