t valid unless the\nresolution between the peaks due to temozolomide acid and \ntemozolomide is not less than 1.5."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/temperature","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Temperature"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Temperature\n(inmin.) \n(°)\n0-2 \n. \n180\n2-22 \n180—>280\n22 - 52 \n280\n- \ninlet port at 290° and detector at 300°,\n- \nflame ionization detector,\n- \nflowrate: 0.68mlperminute,usingheliumornitrogenas \nthe carrier gas.\n- \nsplit ratio: 1:50.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C20H42O. :\nStorage. Store protected from light.\nOestradiol Benzoate\nQsl-hCh \nMol. Wt. 376.5\nOestradiol Benzoate is 17P-hydroxyestra-.l ,3,5(10)-trien-3-yl \nbenzoate.\nOestradiolBenzoate contains not less than 97.0,per cent and \nnot more than 103.0 per cent of C25H28O3, calculated on the \ndried basis. \n......\nCategory. Oestrogen. \n. .\nDescription. Colourless crystals or a white, crystalline powder."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Temperature\n(inmin.) \n(°)\n0-2 \n. \n180\n2-22 \n180—>280\n22 - 52 \n280\n- \ninlet port at 290° and detector at 300°,\n- \nflame ionization detector,\n- \nflowrate: 0.68mlperminute,usingheliumornitrogenas \nthe carrier gas.\n- \nsplit ratio: 1:50.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C20H42O. :\nStorage. Store protected from light.\nOestradiol Benzoate\nQsl-hCh \nMol. Wt. 376.5\nOestradiol Benzoate is 17P-hydroxyestra-.l ,3,5(10)-trien-3-yl \nbenzoate.\nOestradiolBenzoate contains not less than 97.0,per cent and \nnot more than 103.0 per cent of C25H28O3, calculated on the \ndried basis. \n......\nCategory. Oestrogen. \n. .\nDescription. Colourless crystals or a white, crystalline powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Test A may be omitted if tests B and C are carried, out Test C \nmay be omitted if tests A and B are carried out.\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with oestradiol \nbenzoate IPRS or with the reference spectrum of oestradiol \nbenzoate. ■\nB. In the test for Related substances, the principal spot in the \nchromatogram obtained with test solution (b) corresponds to \nthat in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) \nwhen examined in daylight and under ultraviolet light at \n365 nm. \n-\nC. To about 1 mg add 0.5 ml of a 5 per cent w/v solution of \nammonium molybdate in sulphuric acid', a yellowish green \ncolour develops which exhibits an intense green fluorescence \nwhen examined under ultraviolet light at 365 nm. Add 1 ml of \nsulphuric acid and 9 ml of water; the solution becomes pink \nwith a yellowish fluorescence."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Specific optical rotation (2.4.22).-+ 57.0° to + 63.0°, determined \nin a 1.0 per cent w/v solution in dioxan.\nRelated substances. Determine by thin-layer chromatography \n(2.4.17), coating the plate with silica gelG. ,\nSolvent mixture. 90 volumes of chloroform and 10 volumes \nof methanol.\nMobile phase. A mixture of 90 volumes of toluene and\n10 volumes of ethanol (95 per cent).\nTest solution (a). Dissolve 0.2, g of the substance under \nexamination in 10.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nTest solution'(b). Dissolve 0.1 g of the substance under \nexamination in 100.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (a).. A 0.02 per cent w/v solution of the\nsubstance under examination with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (b). A 0.1 per cent w/v solution of \noestradiol benzoate IPRS with the solvent mixture.\nApply to the plate 5 pl of each solution. After development, \ndry the plate in air until odour of the solvent is no longer \ndetectable, heat at 110° for 10 minutes, spray the plate while \nhot with ethanolic sulphuric acid (20 per cent), heat again at\n3100 \nliliiMitiHMIlt\nOESTRADIOL BENZOATE\nIP 2022\n110° for 10 minutes and examine under.ultraviolet light at \n365 nm. Any secondary spot in the chromatogram obtained \nwith test solution (a) is not more intense than the spot in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a).\nSulphated ash (2.3.18). Not more than 0.2 per cent, determined \non0.5 g. \n■ - \n.\nLoss on drying (2.4.19). Not more than 0.5 per cent, determined \non 0.5 g by drying in an oven at 105° for 3 hours.\nAssay. Dissolve 25 mg in sufficient ethanol(95 per cent) to \nproduce 250.0 ml. Dilute 10.0 ml to 100.0 ml with ethanol (95 \nper cent) and measure the absorbance of the resulting solution\nat the maximum at about 231 nm (2:4.7). Calculate the content \nof C25H28O3 taking 500 as the specific absorbance at 231 nm.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/teneligliptin-hydrobromide-hydrate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Teneligliptin Hydrobromide Hydrate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TENELIGLIPTIN HYDROBROMIDE HYDRATE\n[P2022 \n....................................................................\n_ flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n„ spectrophotometer set at 270 nm, \n^injection volume: 75 pl.\nrrZT \nRelative Correction\nNan« \n. \n■ „\nAyyWy, \n. retention time factor\n0.63\n2_Azahypoxanthinei \n0.4\npripozolonnde related\ncompound A* \n2 * \n0.5\n1.32\n'fçipp^olomide acid\"’ \n, \n0.9;\nTemozolomide \n1.0\n0.29\n^Vninoimidazolecarboxamide4 \n1.4\nCyanotcmozolomide2 \n2.3\ni4a55.aihydro-4H -imidazo[4,5-d][l,2,3]triazin-4-one, ' \n■\nU-diazo-4H -imidazole-5-carboxamide, (This is a process impurity and \ninclude'for peak identification only),\n’3’Htethyl-4-pxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5il-d][l,2,3,5]tetrazine -8- \ncarboxylic acid,\n45-aminoimidazole-4-carb oxamide,\nJ3-methyl-4-oxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5,l-d][l,2,3,5]tetrazine-8- \ncarbonitrile (This is a process impurity and include for peak identification\nonly). ' \n.\nInject reference solution (c) and (d). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to temozolomide and \naminoimidazole carboxamide is not less than 2.5 in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) and the \nsignal tp. noise ratio is not less than 10 in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (d).\nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 2.5 times the retention time of the principal \npeak for the test solution. The area of any peak corresponding \nto2-azahypoxanthine is not more than 0.4 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (0.4 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding \nto temozolamide acidis not more than 0.2 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (0.2 per cent), the area of any other secondary \npe^kis pot more than 0,2 times the area of the principal peak in \nthechromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (0.2\nper cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks \nother than peaks corresponding to. ternozolamide related \ncompound A and cyanotemozQlamide is not more than twice \nthe area of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (b) (2.0 per cent). Ignore any peak with \nah area Ibs's than 0.05 times the area of the principalpeak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (0.05 per \ncent). ; \ns .A ■"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TENELIGLIPTIN HYDROBROMIDE HYDRATE\n[P2022 \n....................................................................\n_ flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n„ spectrophotometer set at 270 nm, \n^injection volume: 75 pl.\nrrZT \nRelative Correction\nNan« \n. \n■ „\nAyyWy, \n. retention time factor\n0.63\n2_Azahypoxanthinei \n0.4\npripozolonnde related\ncompound A* \n2 * \n0.5\n1.32\n'fçipp^olomide acid\"’ \n, \n0.9;\nTemozolomide \n1.0\n0.29\n^Vninoimidazolecarboxamide4 \n1.4\nCyanotcmozolomide2 \n2.3\ni4a55.aihydro-4H -imidazo[4,5-d][l,2,3]triazin-4-one, ' \n■\nU-diazo-4H -imidazole-5-carboxamide, (This is a process impurity and \ninclude'for peak identification only),\n’3’Htethyl-4-pxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5il-d][l,2,3,5]tetrazine -8- \ncarboxylic acid,\n45-aminoimidazole-4-carb oxamide,\nJ3-methyl-4-oxo-3,4-dihydroimidazo[5,l-d][l,2,3,5]tetrazine-8- \ncarbonitrile (This is a process impurity and include for peak identification\nonly). ' \n.\nInject reference solution (c) and (d). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to temozolomide and \naminoimidazole carboxamide is not less than 2.5 in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) and the \nsignal tp. noise ratio is not less than 10 in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (d).\nInject reference solution (b) and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 2.5 times the retention time of the principal \npeak for the test solution. The area of any peak corresponding \nto2-azahypoxanthine is not more than 0.4 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (0.4 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding \nto temozolamide acidis not more than 0.2 times the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b) (0.2 per cent), the area of any other secondary \npe^kis pot more than 0,2 times the area of the principal peak in \nthechromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (0.2\nper cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks \nother than peaks corresponding to. ternozolamide related \ncompound A and cyanotemozQlamide is not more than twice \nthe area of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (b) (2.0 per cent). Ignore any peak with \nah area Ibs's than 0.05 times the area of the principalpeak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b) (0.05 per \ncent). ; \ns .A ■"},{"name":"Tests","text":"^Cteriai endotoxins (2.2.3): Not more than 0.88 Endotoxin \npnite.permg of temozolomide. \n' ‘\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14) as \ndescribed under Related substances with the following \nmodifications. \n,\nInject reference solution (a). Thhtest is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation of replicate injections is not more than 1.0 per cent.\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C6H6N602 in the injection.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture, at a \ntemperature2° to 8°..... \n. . ,\nTeneligliptin Hydrobroniide Hydrate\no\nC22H30N6OS, 2Yz HBr, xH2O \nMol.Wt.628.9\nTeneligliptin Hydrobromide Hydrate is {(25’,4.S')-4-| 4-(3-methyl-\n1-phenyl-177-pyrazol-5-yl)piperazine-l-yl]pyrfolidine-2-yl} \n(l;3-thiazolidine-3-yl) methanone hemipentahydrobromide \nhydrate.\nTeneligliptin Hydrobromide Hydrate contains not less than \n98 .0 per cent and not more than 102.0 per cent of C22H3oN6OS,\n2*A HBr, calculated on the anhydrous basis.\nCategory. Antidiabetic. .\nDescription. An off white to cream coloured powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2-4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with teneligliptin \nhydrobromide hydrate IPRS or with the reference spectrum \nof teneligliptin hydrobromide hydrate. / .\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the réference solution.\nHydrobromic acid content. Nbt less than 28.0 per cent w/w \nand not more than 34.0 per cent w/w; calculated on the \nanhydrous basis, determine by liquid chromatography\nTENELIGLIPTIN’HYDROBROMIDE HYDRATE\n(2.4-14), as described under: Assay with, following \nmodifications.: \n: >: ' \nE ••-.bi:;?\nReference solution.. A 0.003 per cent w/v solution of \nhydro bromicac id IPRSin'the¡Solventmixture. \n-Em ■\nCalculate the content ofHBr, :'\" r ' \ni/