djusting the pH to 3.8 with glacial acetic \nacid,\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nB. a mixture of 20 volumes of the buffer \nsolution and 80 volumes of acetonitrile, \n- flow rate: 1.5 ml per minute, \n-\na gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- spectrophotometer set at 260 nm,\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Use the filtrate. Dilute the filtrate, if necessary, \nwith the dissolution medium.\nB. methanol, \n-\nflow rate: 1.5 ml per minute, \n-\na gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n-\nspectrophotometer set at 260 nm, \n-\ninjection volume: 20 pl.\nReference solution. A solution containing 0.03 per cent w/v \neach of lamivudine RS and tenofovir disoproxil fumarate RS \nprepared by dissolving in a mixture of equal volumes of \nmethanol and water and diluted with the dissolution medium.\ninjection volume: 10 pl.\nTime \n(in min.)\nMobile phase A\nMobile phase B\n(per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v) \n0 \n94 \n6 \n3 \n94 \n6 \n5 \n50 \n50 \n8 \n35 \n65 \n9 \n94 \n6 \n12 \n94 \n6\nTime \t\nMobile phase A \t\nMobile phase B \n(in min.) \t\n(per cent v/v) \t\n(per cent v/v) \n0 \n95 \n5\nUse chromatographic system as described in the Assay.\nThe retention time of tenofovir disoproxil is about 4.5 minutes \nand lamivudine is about 1.3 minutes.\n10 \n50 \n50\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates for \ntenofovir disoproxil and 800 theoretical plates for lamivudine \npeak. The tailing factor for both lamivudine and tenofovir \ndisoproxil peaks is not more than 2.0.\n25 \n50 \n50 \n50 \n20 \n80\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0, the column efficiency in not \nless than 2000 theoretical plates  for the peak due to tenofovir \ndisoproxil, 500 theoretical plates for the peak due to \nemtricitabine and the relative standard deviation for replicate \ninjections is not more than 2.0 per cent for each component.\n60 \n95 \n5\n75 \n95 \n5\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nInject reference solution (a). The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates and \nthe tailing factor is not more than 2.0.\nCalculate the content of lamivudine, C,FI II N303S, and tenofovir \ndisoproxil fumarate, Ci9H30N5010P,C4H404 in the medium.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nInject reference solutions (b), (c) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than 3.5 times the area of the peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with the reference solution (b)\nD. Not less than 75 per cent of the stated amount  of lamivudine, \nC K I-I II N 30 3S and tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, \nC 9H30N50 0P,C 4H 40 4 .\nCalculate the contents of C 19 H 30N 50 10P,C 4H 404 and \nCsH,,,FN303S in the tablets.\nFor efavirenz-\nStorage. Store  protected from moisture, at a temperature not \nexceeding 30°.\n(3.5 per cent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary  peaks \nis not more than 6 times the area of the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution (b) \n(6.0 per cent). Ignore the peak corresponding to the peak in \nthe chromatogram obtained in the reference solution (c).\nApparatus No. 1, \nMedium. 1000 ml of 2.0 per cent w/v solution ofsodium lauryl \nsulphate solution, \nSpeed and time. 75 rpm and 60 minutes.\nTenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate, \nLamivudine and Efavirenz Tablets\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under the Tablets.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14)."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tenofovir-disoproxil-fumarate-lamivudine-and-efavirenz-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tenofovir Disoprox