ed with \noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm) (Such \nas Inertsil ODS 3V), -\n- \nmobile phase: a mixture of 60 volumes of a buffer solution \nprepared by dissolving 7.8 g of sodium dihydrogen \northophosphate in 1000 ml of water, adding 1 ml of \ntriethylamine and adjusted to pH 2.3 ; with \northophosphoric acid (10per cent v/v), and 40 volumes \nof acetonitrile,\n- \nflow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- \nspectrophotometer set at 260 nm,\n- \ninjection volume: 10 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0, the column efficiency in not\nless than 2000 theoretical plates and the relative standard \ndéviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per’cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C|9ni0N5OloP/TJTiO^in the tablets:\nStorage. Store protected from moisture, at a temperature not \nexceeding30°. \nr;;\nTENOFOVIR AND. EMTRICITABINE TABLETS ; :"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tenofovir-disoproxil-fumarate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate salt of bis(isopropyloxy- \ncarbonyloxymethyl ester of (/?)-9-(2-phosphonomethoxy- \npropyl)adenine with fumaric acid.\nTenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate contain not less than 97.0 per \ncent and not more than 102.0 per cent of Ci9H30N5OloP5C4Ht04, \ncalculated on the anhydrous basis.\nDescription. A white to off- white crystalline powder.\nA. Determirieby infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the, spectrum with ithat obtained with tenofovir \ndisoproxil fumarate IPRS or with the reference spectruin of \ntenofovir disoproxiffumarate. :\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nRelated substances. Determine.by liquid chromatography \n(2Ai4)y:;.‘7;'',....1\nBuffer' solution. Dissolve 3.5 g of potassium dihydrogen \nphosphate and V.7 g of tertabutyl\"ammonium hydrogen\nsulphate in 800 mlof water, adjusted to pH 6.0 with IM sodium \nhydroxide arid dilute to 1000 ml with water.\nTest solution.. Dissolve 10 mg of the substance under \nexamination in water and dilute to 10.0 ml with water.\nReference solution (a), A.0.0005 per cent w/v solution of \ntenofovir disoproxil fumarate IPRS in waler.\nReference solution (b). Dissolve 10 mg.of fumaric acid in\n50.0ml ofw/er. \n;\nReference solution (c). .Heat the test solution in a boiling \nwater-bath for 20 minutes.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\n- octadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- coluirin temperature: 30°, \n’\nsample temperature: 6°.\n- mobile phase: A. a mixture of 2 volumes of acetonitrile,\n20 volumes of the buffer solution and 78 volumes of\n’ water. ■ ■ ■ \n................ 1 ■ \n' \"7 ’ ’ \n'\nB. a mixture of 65 volumes of acetonitrile, \n20 volumes of the buffer solution and 15 volumes of \nwafer, \n; ■■\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minutes, r’t: ' :1\n- spectrophotometer set at 260;nm, \n< ;\ninjection volume: 20 pl. :i. j \n■■ . ."},"sections":[{"name":"TENOFOVIR DISOPROXIL FUMARATE","text":"Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate salt of bis(isopropyloxy- \ncarbonyloxymethyl ester of (/?)-9-(2-phosphonomethoxy- \npropyl)adenine with fumaric acid.\nTenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate contain not less than 97.0 per \ncent and not more than 102.0 per cent of Ci9H30N5OloP5C4Ht04, \ncalculated on the anhydrous basis.\nDescription. A white to off- white crystalline powder.\nA. Determirieby infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the, spectrum with ithat obtained with tenofovir \ndisoproxil fumarate IPRS or with the reference spectruin of \ntenofovir disoproxiffumarate. :\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nRelated substances. Determine.by liquid chromatography \n(2Ai4)y:;.‘7;'',....1\nBuffer' solution. Dissolve 3.5 g of potassium dihydrogen \nphosphate and V.7 g of tertabutyl\"ammonium hydrogen\nsulphate in 800 mlof water, adjusted to pH 6.0 with IM sodium \nhydroxide arid dilute to 1000 ml with water.\nTest solution.. Dissolve 10 mg of the substance under \nexamination in water and dilute to 10.0 ml with water.\nReference solution (a), A.0.0005 per cent w/v solution of \ntenofovir disoproxil fumarate IPRS in waler.\nReference solution (b). Dissolve 10 mg.of fumaric acid in\n50.0ml ofw/er. \n;\nReference solution (c). .Heat the test solution in a boiling \nwater-bath for 20 minutes.\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\n- octadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- coluirin temperature: 30°, \n’\nsample temperature: 6°.\n- mobile phase: A. a mixture of 2 volumes of acetonitrile,\n20 volumes of the buffer solution and 78 volumes of\n’ water. ■ ■ ■ \n................ 1 ■ \n' \"7 ’ ’ \n'\nB. a mixture of 65 volumes of acetonitrile, \n20 volumes of the buffer solution and 15 volumes of \nwafer, \n; ■■\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minutes, r’t: ' :1\n- spectrophotometer set at 260;nm, \n< ;\ninjection volume: 20 pl. :i. j \n■■ . ."},{"name":"TENOFOVIR DISOPROXIL FUMARATE","text":"Time Mobile phase A Mobile phase B\n, \n■ (in min) (per cent v/v) ; : \n; (per cent v/v) l\n- \nk 19 - - .- C f. b i\n.1 MO J, ^9 \n.■■■ \n51\n60 \n0 \n; \n•• 100 ’i:\n65 \n0 \n100\n70,. \n: \n81 - :io ■/ ,b •/./ / 19 \n.... ;\n80 \n81 \n19\nThe relative retention time with reference TÒ tenófovir \ndisoproxil fumarate for tenofovir monoester is about O.5., .\nInject reference solution (c). The test is: hot valid unless the \nresolution between the tenofovir disoproxil fumarate peak and \ntenofovir monoester peak is not less than 25.0.; -\nInject referente solution (a),