3.0 with orthophosphoric\nacid and 40 volumes of acetonitrile, \nWjbsflbwrate: 1.8 ml per minute,\n( per cent v/v)\n— spectrophotometer set at 220 nm,\nJA\n¿fl\n- injection volume: 50 pl.\nu\nOu\n2\n4Ti\n70\nName \nRelative Correction\no\nJv\n/u\n■ \nretention time factor\n18\n30\n70\nA'-Methy1-1 -(naphthalene-1 -yl)\n24\n16\n84 '\nmethanamine \n0.14 \n0.67\n26\n5\n95\nTerbinafine \n1.0 \n—\n30\n0\n100\nUnknown \n— \n1.0\n37\n40\n■ 60\nTotal impurity \n— \n—\n45\n40\n60\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 10.0 per \n¿enE'\"\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram with the test solution, the area of impurity due \nto A-Methyl-1-( naphthalene- 1-yl) is not more than 0.57 times \nthe area of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwithrefercnce solution (0.2 per cent), the area of any secondary \npeak is not more than 0.57 times the area of the principal peak \nih the:chromatogram obtained with reference solution (0.2 per \ncent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary peaks is \nnot more than 2 times the area of the peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with reference solution (0.7 per cent).\nLimit of Terbinafine Dimer. Determine by liquid \nchromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. 40 volumes of acetonitrile and TO volumes \nof water.\nfest solution. Shake a quantity of the powdered tablets \ncontaining 250 mg of terbinafine with 50 ml of, the solvent \nfixture, and mix with the aid of ultrasound for 20. minutes, \ndilute to 166.0 ml with solvent mixture and filter.\nReference solution. A solution of terbinafine hydrochloride \nfPRS in the solvent mixture containing 0.00014 per cent w/v of\nterbinafine.\nTERBINAFINE TABLETS\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous:silica,(5 pm),\n- column temperature: 52°, \n• \n.■\n- mobile phase: A. 1.0 ml of triethylgmine in 1000.0 ml of\nwater, ■ \n■ .<\nB. 1.0 ml of triethylamine in a 1000.0 ml \nof a mixture of 19 volumes of acetonitrile and 1 volume \nof water,\n- - a gradient programme using the conditions given below, \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n■ spectrophotometer set at 280 nm,\n- injection volume: 100 pl,\n. Time\nMobile phase B\nMobile phase A\n( per cent v/v)\n(in min.)\nCorrection\nName\nRelative \nretention time\nfactor\nTerbinafine\n1.0\nTerbinafine dimer1\n2.0\n0.48\n'(2E ,4E )-4-(4,4-Dirnethylpent-2-ynylidene)-jV7, W-dimethyl-W N5- \nbis(naphthalen-l-ylmethyl)pent-2-ene-l, 5-diamine.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 10.0 per \ncent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution. In the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of \nimpurity due to terbinafine diamer is not more than 0.9 times \nthe area of the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (0.05 percent). ■\nOther tests. Comply with 'the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14);\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Shake a .quantity \nof the powder containing 20 mg of Terbinafine with 50 ml of \nthe mobile phase and mix with, the aid of ultrasound for \n20 minutes, dilute to 100.0 ml with the mobile phase and filter.\nReference solution; A 0^022J per cent w/v solution of \nterbinafine hydrochloride IPRS in the mobile phase. >\n■unKHUTAIilNE SULPHATE\nChromatographic system \n\"\n'': - a stainless steel column 15 cm x 3.9 mm, packed with\noctaylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 urn),\n- mobile phase: 60 volumes of a buffer solution prepared\n■' > by dissolving 0.85 g of monobasic potassium phosphate\nand 1,0 g of sodium 1-decanesulfonate in 1000 ml of \nwater and adjusted to pH 3.0 with orthophosphoric\n;; : acidand 40 volumes of acetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1.8 ml per minute,\n7 - < spectrophotometer set at 220 nm, ■ -; - r\n- injection volume: 5 pl. ■ \n■\nInject the reference solution! The test is not valid unless the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is hot more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C^JTsNin the tablets.\nStorage. Store protected from light and moisture.\nLabelling. The label states the. strength in terms of the \nequivalent amount of terbinafine."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/terbutaline-inhalation","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Terbutaline Inhalation"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Terbutaline Inhalation\nTerbutaline Sulphate Inhalation; Terbutaline Inhalation \nAerosol (Terbutaline Sulphate Inhalation Aerosol\nTerbutaline Inhalation is a suspension of Terbutaline Sulphate,\näs^a' superfine powder, in a suitable liquid in a suitable \npressurised container. It may contain suitable pharmaceutical \naids such as-surfactants, stabilising agents, etc. '\nTerbutaline Inhalation delivers riot less than 75.0 per cent and\nnot more than 125.0 per cent of the stated amount of terbutaline \n»>>Ptate.(C12H19NO3)2,H2SO4, per inhalation, by actuation of \nthe valve.\nMsual strength. 250 pg in each metered dose."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Terbutaline Inhalation\nTerbutaline Sulphate Inhalation; Terbutaline Inhalation \nAerosol (Terbutaline Sulphate Inhalation Aerosol\nTerbutaline Inhalation is a suspension of Terbutaline Sulphate,\näs^a' superfine powder, in a suitable liquid in a suitable \npressurised container. It may contain suitable pharmaceutical \naids such as-surfactants, stabilising agents, etc. '\nTerbutaline Inhalation delivers riot less than 75.0 per cent and\nnot more than 125.0 per cent of the stated amount of terbutaline \n»>>Ptate.(C12H19NO3)2,H2SO4, per inhalation, by actuation of \nthe valve.\nMsual strength. 250 pg in each metered dose."},{"name":"identification","text":"determine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4.17), coating the \nPlate with silica gel GF254. , \n. . : \n. ..\n, TERBUTALINE: INHALATION\nMobile phase. A mixture of 65 volumes :pts2hpropanol, \n25 volumes of cyclohexane and 5 volumes of formic acid.\nTest solution. Remove the actuator from the pressurised \ncontainer, shake the container for about 30 seconds and place \nit in an inverted position in a small beaker containing 5 ml of \nwater. Discharge a sufficient number of deliveries containing \n5 mg of Terbutaline Sulphate, under the surface of the solvent.\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution of terbutaline \nsulphate IPRSic water.\nApply to the plate 2 pl of each solution. After development, \ndry the plate in air, spray with a 2 per cent w/v solution of \n4-aminoantipyrine ip methanol. Examine in daylight and under \nultraviolet light at 365 nm. The principal spot in the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution corresponds to \nspot in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution.\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Inhalation \nPreparations (Pressurised metered-dose Preparations);\nFollow the procedure described under Assay wherever the \namount of active substance is to be determined in any test.\nAssay. Carry out the test for Content of active ingredient \ndelivered per actuation stated under Inhalation Preparations \n(Pressurised metered-dose Preparations). ,\nUse 35 ml of water and finally dilute to 50.0 ml with water. \nDilute.a.suitable volume of the solution with water to produce \na solution containing 50 pg of Terbutaline Sulphate per ml. To\n10.0 ml of the solution in a 50-ml volumetric flask add 35 ml of \nbuffer solution pH9.5. and 1.0 ml of 4-aminoantipyrine \nsolution. Mix, add 1.0 ml oipotassium ferricyanide,solution \nwith, vigorous swirling of the flask, dilute to volume with water \nand.mix.Exactly 75 seconds after the additionpf thepotoi^ifrm \nferricyanide.so lution measure the absorbance of the resulting\nsolution at the maximum at about 550 nm (2.4.7), using as the \nblank a solution prepared in the same manner using 10.0 ml o f \nwater in place of the solution of the substance under \nexamination. \n•• • \n■\nCalculate the Content of (e!2Hj9NO3)2,H2SO4 in the solution \nfrom the absorbance obtained by repeating the operation using \na solution containing 100 pg of lerbutciline sulphate IP RS in \nplace of the solution of the substance under examination.\nCalculate the amount of (C^HigNC^H^SO^ delivered per \nactuation of the valve. ..... ... \n, \n.. i(\nDetermine the content of active ingredient a second and third \ntime by repeating theprocedure on the middle ten and on the \nlast ten successive combined actuations of the valve. For \neach of the three determinations the average content of \n(CnH i9NO3)2,fI2SO4 delivered per actuation of the valve meets \nthe requirements. \n-v.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture at a temperature not \ncxcecding30°.\nLabelling. The* label states the amount of active ingredient \ndelivered per inhalation. \n-"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/terbutaline-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Terbutaline Injection"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Terbutaline Injection\nTerbutaline Sulphate Injection\nTerbutaline Injection, is; a> sterile solution of Terbutaline \nSulphate in Water for Injections.\nTerbutaline Injection contains riot less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of terbutaline \nsulphate (Ci2Hi9NÔ3)2, H2SO:.\nUsual strength. 500 pg per ml."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Terbutaline Injection\nTerbutaline Sulphate Injection\nTerbutaline Injection, is; a> sterile solution of Terbutaline \nSulphate in Water for Injections.\nTerbutaline Injection contains riot less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of terbutaline \nsulphate (Ci2Hi9NÔ3)2, H2SO:.\nUsual strength. 500 pg per ml."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Determine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4.17), coating the \nplate with silica gel G .\nMobile phase.. Amixture of 65 volumes of 2-propanol, \n25 volumes of cyclohexane and 5 volumes of formic acid.\nTest solution. Use the injection.\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution of terbutaline \nsulphate JPRS in saline, solution.\nApply to the plate 2 pl of each solution. After development,\ndry the plate in air, spray with a 2 per cent w/v solution of \n4-dminoàntipyriné in methanol. Dry the plate in air and spray \nwith a freshly prepared 8.0 per cent w/v solution ofpotassium \nferricyanide in a1 mixture of 4 volumes of strong ammonia\nsolution and 1 volume of water. The principal spot in the \nchromatogram obtained with thé test solution corresponds to \nspot in thé chromatogram obtained with the reference solution.\nTests “ ’ <\npH (2.4.24). 3.0 to 5.0. \n.... .\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2:3). Not more than 1250.0,Endotoxin\nUnits per mg of terbutaline.sulphate. \n:■-■■■\nOther tests. Comply with thé tests stated under Parenteral \npreparations (Injections):\nAssay. Measure a volume containing about 5 mg of Terbutaline\nSulphate and add sufficient water to produce 50.0 ml. To \n5.0ml add 35 ml of a buffer solution prepared by dissolving \n36.3 g of tris (hydroxymethyl), aminomethane in 900 ml of \nwater., adjusted to pH.bétween 9.4 and 9.6 and adding sufficient \nwaterto produce 1000 rril. Add 1.0 ml of a freshly prepared 2.0 \nper.cent w/v.sblution of 4-aminoaniipyrine, mix.'and add 1.0 \nml of a freshly prepared 8.0 per cent w/v solution ofpotassium\nIP2Ô22\nTERBUTALINE INJECTION\nferricyanide with vigorous swirling and sufficient ofthe buff •\nsolution to produce 50.0 ml. Exactly 75; seconds;after the \naddition of the potassium ferricyanide solution measure the \nabsorbance of the resulting solution at the maximum at about \n550 nm (2.4.7), using water as the blank. \nJ /!\nCalculate the content of (Cl2Hi9NO3)2, H2SO4 from the \nabsorbance obtained by repeating the operation using a 0 01 \nper cent w/v solution of terbutaline sulphate IPRS and \nbeginning at the words “To 5.0ml add35 ml......”. \n;.,\nStorage. Store protected from light, in single dose containers\nLabelling...The label states that the injection should not be \nused if the solution is discoloured. ; ; 1 ,; \n...: /"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/terbutaline-sulphate-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Terbutaline Sulphate Injection"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Terbutaline Sulphate Injection\nTerbutaline Injection is a sterile solution of Terbutaline\nSulphate in Water for Injections.\nTerbutaline Injection contains not less than 90.0 per cent and\nnot more than 110.0 per cent ofthe stated amount ofterbutaline\nsulphate (CI2HI9N03)2, H2S04•\nUsual strength. 500 Ilg per m!."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Terbutaline Sulphate Injection\nTerbutaline Injection is a sterile solution of Terbutaline\nSulphate in Water for Injections.\nTerbutaline Injection contains not less than 90.0 per cent and\nnot more than 110.0 per cent ofthe stated amount ofterbutaline\nsulphate (CI2HI9N03)2, H2S04•\nUsual strength. 500 Ilg per m!."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Determine by thin-layer chromatography (2.4. I7), coating the\nplate with silica gel G\nMobile phase. A mixture of 65 volumes of 2-propanol,\n25 volumes of cyclohexane and 5 volumes ofjormic acid.\nTest solution. Use the injection.\nTERBUTALINE INJECTION\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution ofterbutaline\nsulphate RS in saline solution.\nApply to the plate 2 III of each solution. After development,\ndry the plate in air, spray with a 2 per cent w/v solution of\n4-aminoantipyrine in methanol. Dry the plate in air and spray\nwith a freshly prepared 8.0 per cent w/v solution ofpotassium\nferricyanide in a mixture of 4 volumes of strong ammonia\nsolution and 1 volume of water. The principal spot in the\nchromatogram obtained with the test solution corresponds to\nthat in the chromatogram obtainedwith the reference solution."},{"name":"Tests","text":"pH(2.4.24). 3.0to 5.0.\nOther tests. Complies with the tests stated under Parenteral\npreparations (Injections).\nAssay. Measure accurately a volume containing about 5 mg\nof Terbutaline Sulphate and add sufficient water to produce\n50.0 m!. To 5.0 ml add 35 ml ofa buffer solution prepared by\ndissolving 36.3 g of tris (hydroxymethyl) aminomethane in\n900 ml ofwater, adjusting the pH to between 9.4 and 9.6 and\nadding sufficient water to produce 1000 m!. Add 1.0 ml of a\nfreshly\nprepared\n2.0\nper\ncent\nw/v\nsolution\nof\n4-aminoantipyrine, mix and add 1.0 ml of a freshly prepared\n8.0 per cent w/v solution of potassium ferricyanide with\nvigorous swirling and sufficient of the buffer solution to\nproduce 50.0 m!. Exactly 75 seconds after the addition ofthe\npotassium ferricyanide solution measure the absorbance of\nthe resulting solution at the maximum at about 550 nm (2.4.7),\nusing water as the blank.\nCalculate the content of (CI2HI9N03)2, H2S04 from the\nabsorbance obtained by repeating the operation using a 0.01\nper cent w/v solution of terbutaline sulphate RS and\nbeginning at the words \"To 5.0 ml add 35 ml......\".\nStorage. Store protected from light, in single dose containers.\nLabelling. The label states that the injection should not be\nused\" if the solution is discoloured."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/terbutaline-sulphate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Terbutaline Sulphate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Terbutaline Sulphate\n(Cï2H!9NO3)2,H2SO4 ' \n■ Mol. Wt. 548.7\nTerbutaline Sulphate is {^S)-2-(iert--bûtÿlamiiio)“l\"(3,5-\