lution the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (1.0 \nper cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary peaks\nis not more than twice the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (2.0 per \ncent). Ignore the peak due to tartaric acid corresponding to \nthe peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (b).\nUniformity of content. Complies with the test stated under \nTablets.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14), as described \nunder Assay using following modification. \n■ :\nTest solution. Disperse 1 intact tablet in the mobile phase with \nthe aid of ultrasound for 20 minutes and dilute to 10.0 ml with \nthe mobile phase, filter. Dilute further with the mbbile phase if \nnecessary. \n■■\nCalculate the content of C^H37NQ7-in the tablet. \n• ?: w -\nOther tests. Comply with the; tests stated under Tablets. . ■\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4,14).\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof powder containing 10 mgofTolterodiric Tartrate in 70 ml of \nthe mobile phase with1 the aid of ultrasound for 20 minutes and \ndilute to 100.0 ml with the mobile phase, filter.\nReference solution. A 0.01 per cent w/v solution of lolterodine \ntartrate IPRS in thé mobile phase. 1 \n; ■ \n।\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 25 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n•T- mobile phase: ainixtiire of 65 volumes of buffer solution \nprepared by mixing 2.2 ml of orthophosphoric acid to\n1000 ml with water, adjusted to pH 3.0 with triethylamine \nand 35 volumes of acetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1.5 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 280 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 p. I. s \n. \n1\nTOLVAPTAN • ■; , /..■\nInj ect the reference solution. The test is. not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 ^theoreticalplates, the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation fop replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the content of C26H37NO7 in the tablets.\nStorage. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tolterodine-tartrate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tolterodine Tartrate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"TOLTERODINE TARTRATE\nchloroform, filtering eachiinto the flask. Add chloroform to \nvolume and mix (Solution A)wDilute 25 ml of the solution with \nchloroform to 100 mland mix. Measure the absorbance.of the \nresulting solution at the maximum at about 258 nm (2.4.7), \nusing 0.001 per cent w/v solution of tolnaftate IPRS in \nchloroform.\nCalculate the content of C19H)7NOS in topical solution.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture..; v - .: v :\nTolterodine Tartrate\nC22H3 ¡NO, CiHA \nMol Wt. 475.6\nTolterodineTartrate is 2-[(17?)-3-[bis(l-methylethyl)amino]-\n1 -phenylpropyl]-4-methylphenol tartrate.\nTolterodine Tartrate contains not less than 98.0 per cent and \nnot more than 102.0 per cent of \n¡NO,C4H6O6 ^calculated\non the dried basis.\nCategory. Anticholinergic.\nDescription. A white to off-white crystalline powder t\nA. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6).\nCompare the spectrum with that obtained;with tqlterpfine \ntartrate IPRS or with the reference; spectrum.of tolterodine \ntartrate.. \n.. \nfu\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution. ■ ; '"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"TOLTERODINE TARTRATE\nchloroform, filtering eachiinto the flask. Add chloroform to \nvolume and mix (Solution A)wDilute 25 ml of the solution with \nchloroform to 100 mland mix. Measure the absorbance.of the \nresult