ene-13-D-fructo-\npyranose sulphamate.\nTopiramate contains not less than 98.0 per cent and not more \nthan 102.0 per cent of C l2H2INORS, calculated on the anhydrous \nbasis.\nCategory. Anti-convul sant.\nDose. 25 mg daily.\nDescription. A white to off-white powder."},{"name":"Identification","text":"A. Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with topiramate RS \nor with the reference spectrum of topiramate.\nB. Melting range (2.4.21). 120° to 130°."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Specific optical rotation (2.4.22). -28.0° to-36.0°, determined \nin a 0.4 per cent w/v solution in methanol at 20°.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14).\nTest solution. Weigh 0.4 g of the substance under examination \nand dissolve in 10 ml of a mixture of 50 volumes of water and \n50 volumes of acetonitrile.\nReference solution. A 0.1 per cent w/v solution each of\n(2,3:4,5-Bis-0-(1-methylethylidene)-heta-D-frrIct0pvranose \nRS (topiramate impurity A RS) and 2,3-0-( 1 -methyl-\nethylidene)-beta-D-fructopyranose sulphamate ---.RS \n(topiramate impurity B RS) in the mobile phase.\n!: 1111Fr \nIP 2018 \t\n1p 2018 \nTOPIRAMATE \nTOPOTECAN HYDROCHLORIDE\nChromatographic system"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/topotecan-hydrochloride","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Topotecan Hydrochloride"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Topotecan Hydrochloride\nTopotecan Hydrochloride is (45)-1 ()-| (dimethylamino) methyl} \n4-ethyl-4,9-dihydroxy-l/f-pyrano[3,,4/:6i,7j]ind<iHzino[l!-\nb\\quinoline-3,14(477,1277)-dione hydrochloride. íPa;\nTOPOTECAN HYDROCHLORIDE\nlp2022\ntecan Hydrochloride contains not less than 98.0 per cent \n°dnot more than 102.0 per cent.ofCsaH^NjC^HCl, calculated\non the anhydrous basis.\nCategory.Ant>eancer.\nDescription A light yellow to greenish yellow powder.\nQ^j^jQj^^ top°tecan Hydrochloride is cytotoxic; extra\ncare is required to prevent inhaling particles and exposing\nthe skin tq fl \n'"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Topotecan Hydrochloride\nTopotecan Hydrochloride is (45)-1 ()-| (dimethylamino) methyl} \n4-ethyl-4,9-dihydroxy-l/f-pyrano[3,,4/:6i,7j]ind<iHzino[l!-\nb\\quinoline-3,14(477,1277)-dione hydrochloride. íPa;\nTOPOTECAN HYDROCHLORIDE\nlp2022\ntecan Hydrochloride contains not less than 98.0 per cent \n°dnot more than 102.0 per cent.ofCsaH^NjC^HCl, calculated\non the anhydrous basis.\nCategory.Ant>eancer.\nDescription A light yellow to greenish yellow powder.\nQ^j^jQj^^ top°tecan Hydrochloride is cytotoxic; extra\ncare is required to prevent inhaling particles and exposing\nthe skin tq fl \n'"},{"name":"Identification","text":"A Determine; by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.6). \nCompare the spectrum with that obtained with topotecan \nhydrochloride IPRS or with the reference spectrum of \ntopotecan hydrochloride.\nB. In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram \nobtained with the test solution corresponds to the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution."},{"name":"Tests","text":"pH(2.4.24).3.5 to 4.5, determined in a 1.0 per cent w/v solution.\nSpecific optical rotation (2:422). + 30.0° to + 38.0°, determined\nin a 1.0 per cent w/v solution in methanol.\nTotal chloride. 7.6 per cent to 8.1 per cent.\nWeigh 0.5 g, dissolve in 10 ml of methanol, add 20 ml of water \nand 2^fl\\otglacial acetic acid: Titrate with 0:1 M silver \nnitrate, solution using eosin yellow solution as indicator. \nColour changes from orange to dark pink....\n1 ml of 0.7 M silver nitrate is equivalent to 0.003545 g of Cl.\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(Ul$<hei\nSolvent mixture. 30 volumes of acetonitrile and 70 volumes \nof a buffer solution prepared by diluting 1 ml of trifluoroacetic \nacid in i000 ml of water.\nTest solution.Dissolve 40 nig of the substance under \n«àmihâtîônin100 ml of the solvent mixture. ■\n(a). A 0.04 