r replicate injections isn°t \nmore than 5.0 per cent in the chromatogram obtained with\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography"}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/tranexamic-acid-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Tranexamic Acid Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Tranexamic Acid Tablets\n(2.4.14). ■\n^riexairiic Acid Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent \n^ not more than 110.0 per cent of tranexamic acid, CgH^NOj.\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of the powdered tablets \ncontaining 0.5 g of Tranexamic Acid in the mobile phase with\n3846\n3847\nwww.webofpharma.com\nthe aid of ultrasound for 20 minutes with intermittent shaking \nand dilute to 50.0 ml with the mobile phase.\nReference solution (a). A 0.001 per cent w/v solution of \ntranexamic acid IPRS with the mobile phase..;; ■\nReference solution (b).A solution containing 0.002 per cent \nw/v of tranexamic acid IPRS and 0.0002 per cent w/v of \ntranexamic acid related compound CIPRS with the mobile \nphase. \n■'\nChromatographic system\n- a stainless steel column 10 cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (3.5 pm),\n- mobilephase: amixtiireof85 volumesofa buffer solution\nprepared by dissolving 10.5 g of sodium dihydrogen \nphosphate monohydrate, in 1000 ml of water, add 8 ml\nof triethylamine and 2.3 g of sodium dodecyl sulphate, \nadjusted to pH 2.5 with orthophosphoric acid and 15 \nvolumes of acetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n- spectrophotometer set at 220 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nName\nRelative \nretention time\nTranexamic acid\n1.0\nTranexamic acid related compound C1*\n1.1\nTranexamic acid related compound D3*\n1.2\nTranexamic acid related compound B3\n1.5\nTranexamic acid related compound A4\n2.3\nProcess impurity controlled in the drug substance. It is included for \nidentification purposes only and not be included in the total degradation \nproducts:\n'(RS)'4-(Aminomethyl)cyclohex-l-enecarboxylic acid,\n24-(Aminomethyl)benzoic acid,\n3cis-4-(Aminomethyl)cyclohexanecarboxylic acid,\n4iraKS',rraMS'-4,4'-[Iminobis(niethy[ene)]dicyclohexanecarboxylic acid.\nInject reference solution (a) and (b). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to tranexamic acid and \ntranexamic acid related compound C is not less than 2.0 in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (b), the relative \nstandard deviation for replicate injections is not more than 5.0 \nper cent in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a).\nInject reference solution (a) and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram 5.3 times the retention time of the principal \npeak. The area of any peak corresponding to tranexamic acid \nrelated compound B, multiplied with correction factor of 1.2, \nis hot more than 3 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.3 per \ncent), the area of any peak corresponding to tranexamic acid \nrelated compound A is not more than twice, the area of the\nTRANEXAMIC ACID TABLETS\nIp202)\nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with refem \nsolution (a) (0.2 per cent), the area of any other seconch \npeak is not more than the area of the principal peak joZ\nchromatogram obtained with réference solution (a) (o’¡ \ncent) and the sum of areas of all the secondary peaks not \nmore than 5 times the area of the principal peak in. the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (o^ ^ \ncer-0- \"\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2:4; 14). - 7;s\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse;aquantity \nof the powder containing 0.65 g of Tranexamic Acid inuu/er \nwith the aid of ultrasound for 20 minutes with intermiltent \nshaking and dilute to 250.0 ml with water.■\nReference solution. A0.26 per cent w/v solution of tranexamic \nacid IPRS in water. \n.. ;