per cent w/v solution of \nlithqch^ii^..,(ieid(iPtRS. ( ursodeoxycholic acid impurity C\n2 chenodeoxycholic acid.\n1PRS) in the solvent mixture (Solution A). Dilute 2.0 ml of the \nsolutioii to l00.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nReference solution (c). To 5.0 ml of solution A, add 10 mg of \nchenqdebxychblic acid IPRS (ursodeoxycholic acid impurity \nAIPRS)'apd dilute to 50.0 ml with the solvent mixture.\nApplyttpfheipl^te.S: pi of :each solution.' Allow the mobile \nphase to rise l 5 cm. Dry the plate at 120° for 10 minutes and \nspray immediately with a 4.76 per cent w/v solution of \nphosphomolybdic acid ip a mixture of 1 volume of sulphuric\nand.20, volumes of glacial acetic acid and heat at 120° \n^^bblueiSppts appear on a lighter background. In the \nchrpmatpgram obtained, with reference solution (c), the \nchromatogram shows 2 clearly separated spots. In the \nchromatogram obtained with test solution (a), any spot due to \n^deoxycholicacidimpurilyC is not more intense than the\npnncipal spot in the chromatogram obtained with reference \n^oiifo) (0.1 per cent).\n^^^Iwiahces. Determine by liquid chromatography\nio volumes of methanol and 90 volumes of\n^rcobile;phaSe, .... . ■ . \n. . \n. ... . ,...\nsbltitibh. Dissolve 60 mg of the substance under \nexamination in the solvent mixture and dilute to 20.0 ml with \n!he solvent mixture. ; \n, •"},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"Ursodeoxycholic Acid\nC24H.;o04 \nMol. Wt. 392.6\nUrsodeoxycholic Acid is 3a,7p-dihydroxy-5£-cholan-24-oic \nacid. - e, rmmJw \nrm i.-h. jiBhsæi 'O\nUrsodexoxycholic acid contains not less itiaii 99.0 per cent \nand not more than 10L0 per cent of C24IL0O4, calculated on \nthe dried basis. \n'■\nCategory. Treatment of gallstones. \n.?. <\nDescription À white or almost white powder.\nIdentification ; \n/, \n; uu .\nTests B and Cmay be omitted if test A is carried out. Test A \nmay be omitted if tests B and C are carried out.\nA< Determine by infrared absorption spectrophotometry (2.4.