/."},{"name":"Tests","text":"Dissolution (2.5.2). Complies with the test stated under Tablets.\nRelated substances; Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4.14). ■ \n■' 'v,‘ ’ \n' ” ' : ' ' ' ’ \"\nTest solution. Disperse a quantity of powdered tablets \ncontaining 200 dig of venlafaxine in 80 ml of a 2.4 per cent v/v \nsolution of orthophosphoric acid, with the aid of ultrasound \nfor 30 minutes, cool and dilute to 100.0 ml with water and filter.\nReference solution fa). Dilute 1.0 ml. of the test solution to\n100.0 mlwith mobile phase A and further Dilute, 1.0 ml of the \nsolution to 5.0 ml with mobile phase A.\n3932\nwww.webofpharma.com\nReference solution (b). A 0.2 per cent w/v. solution of \n^lafaxine) impurity IPRS (containing impurity D and F) in \njnobilephaseA;\n^^¿^'sdiutioh (c). Dilute 25.'0 ml of reference solution (a)\nt0100.0 ml with mobile phase A.\nchromatographic system; \n’\n; - a stainless steel column 25 cm * 4.6 mm. packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica, (5 gm), (Such \nas Partisil ODS 3), \n, s\n-v mobile phase: A. amixtureof 1 volume of triethylamine,\n^0 volumes of acetonitrile and. 80 volumes of water \nAdjusted to pH 3.5 with orthophosphoric acid.\n{■- 'Vi :Ai \n' -' B: a mixture of 1 volume of triethylamine,\n50 volumes of acetonitrile and 50 volumes of water \nadjusted to pH 3.5 with orthophosphoric acid.\n~ a gradient programme using the conditions given below,\nflow rate: 1 ml per minute,....\n- spectrophotometer set at 226 nm,\n~ injection volume: 20 pl.\nTime. \nMobile phase A Mobile phase B\n(in min.)\n.. (per cent v/v)\n(per cent v/v)\n0\n100\n0\n\"720 :\n' J 100 ; \n.\n\" 0''\n. .. . 30\n; 0\n. 100..\n■0 ■ ;'\n100\n' 48'\n100\n0\n' 60\n100 ■ \n.\n, 0\nName\" ' \n'' ' Relative\n-■ \nretention time\nVenlafaxine impurity D1 \n0.8\nVenlafaxine (Retention time is about 13 minutes) 1.0\nVenlafaxine impurity F2 \n: 1.7\nt(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-(methylamino) .ethyl] cyclo- \nhcxanol,\n:((2&S)-2-(cycIohex-l-enyl)-2-(4-niethoxy