olution(af Dissolve 50.0 mg of voriconazole IPRS \nip 5,0 ml I Msodium hydroxide, dilute to 10.0 ml with the \nmobile phase. Sonicate if necessary. Allow to stand for \n3iypinutes. Further dilute 1.0 ml of the solution to 100.0 ml \nwith the mobile phase.\nReference solution (b). A solution containing 0.0005 per cent \nwMôf voriconazole impurity BIPRS in thé mobile phase.\nReference solution (c). À solution containing 0.0005 per cent \nvtly of voriconazole IPRS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic system\na stainless steel column 15cm x 4.6 mm, packed with\nJLf!i oçthdecÿsilâne bonded to porous silica (3.0 pm),\ndoiunm'temperature:35°,\nmobile phase: a mixture of 530 volumes of a buffer \nsolution prepared by dissolving 1.9 g of ammonium \nformate ’in 1000 rid of water, adjusted to pH 4.0 with \nformic acid, 157' volumes of acetonitrile and 313\nvolumes of methanol, .\nVORICONAZOLE INJECTION\n- flow rate:-1.4 ml per minute, - ■; ■\n- spectrophotometer set at 256 nm, \n- injection volume: 20pl.\nName ’’\nRelative \nretention time\nCorrection\nfactor\nImpurity A’ \n.\n'L■ ' ! / 025 ;\n; \n02 ’ ; ’\nImpurity B2\n0.6 ;\n, : 2.1 .. ■ ,\nImpurity C3\n0.3 \n: ■\n0.7\nVoriconazole\n1.0\n—\n1 l-(2,4-Difluorophenyl)-2-( 1H-1,2,4-triazol- l-yl)ethanone,\n?(2RS,3SR)-2-(2,4-i)ifluorophcnyl)-3-pyrimidin-4-yl-l-(lH;l,2,4- \ntriazol-l-yl)butan-2-oJ,\nM-Ethyl-5-fltioropyrimidine.\nInject reference solution (a).The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between impurity A and impurity C is not less than\n1.8. Inject reference solution (b) tb identify imptirity B,\nInject reference solution (c)and the test solution.; In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is hot more than thearea1 of the principal peak \nin the chromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) \n(0.5 per cent) and sum of areas of all the secondary peaks is \nnot more than 4 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) (2.0 per \ncent).\nBacterial endotoxins (2.2.3). Not more than 0,1 Endotoxins \nUnit per mg of voriconazole (for intravenous bolus injection) \nand not more than 1.5 Endotoxins Units per mg of voriconazole \n(for intravenous infusion).\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTest solution. Mix the content of 10 containers. Dissolve a \nquantity of the powder tb obtain a solution containing' 0.2 per \ncent w/v of Voriconazole in the mobile phase. Further dilute\n1,0 ml of the solution to 50.0 mi with the mobile phase.,..\nReference solution. A 0.004 per cent w/v-solution of\nvoriconazole IPRS in the mobile phase.\nChromatographic systems\n- a stainless column 25 cm x 4,6 mm, packed with\noctadecysilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm),\n- mobile phase: a mixture of 520 volumes of a buffer\nsolution prepared by dissolving 11.62 g \ntetramethylethyldiamine in 1000 ml water, adjusted to \npH 7.0 with orthophosphoric pen/and 480 volumes of \nacetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute,\n- spectrophotometer set at 254 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 ul. :\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2500, theoretical plates, and \nthe tailing factor is not more than 2.0."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/voriconazole-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Voriconazole Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"VORICONAZOLE-TABLETS\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.7■- ;\nCalculate the content of C;6H l4l;3N5() in'theinjection.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture, at a temperature not \nexceeding30°. \n'\nLabelling. The label states (1) direction for constituting the \nsolution; (2) the name of any added buffering agent or \npharmaceutical aids; (3)’ strength in terms of the equivalent \namount of Voriconazole.\nVoriconazole Tablets\nVoriconazole Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of \nvoriconazole,C:61 I^FjNjO. ” \n: :\nUsual strengths,. 50 mg; 200 mg."},"sections":[{"name":"PREAMBLE","text":"VORICONAZOLE-TABLETS\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.7■- ;\nCalculate the content of C;6H l4l;3N5() in'theinjection.\nStorage. Store protected from moisture, at a temperature not \nexceeding30°. \n'\nLabelling. The label states (1) direction for constituting the \nsolution; (2) the name of any added buffering agent or \npharmaceutical aids; (3)’ strength in terms of the equivalent \namount of Voriconazole.\nVoriconazole Tablets\nVoriconazole Tablets contain not less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of \nvoriconazole,C:61 I^FjNjO. ” \n: :\nUsual strengths,. 50 mg; 200 mg."},{"name":"Identification","text":"In the Assay, the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith the test solution; corresponds to, the peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with the reference solution,.\nTests '\nApparatus No. 2 (Paddle), - - ; ; '\nMedium. 900 ml of 0.1 Mhydrochloric acid, \nSpeed and time. 75 rp nr and 45 minutes.\nDissolution (2.5.2).\nWithdraw a suitable volume of the medium and filter.\nDetermine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nTestsolytipn.- Use the filtrate and dilute, if necessary, with the \ndissolution medium- /\nReference solution. Dissolve a quantity of voriconazole IPRS\nin methanol and dilute with the dissolution medium to obtain \na solution of the same concentration as that of the test solution.\nUse chromatographic system as described under.Assay.\nInject the reference solution and the test solution.\nCalculate the,content of Cl(rH A?.ìNsO in the medium.\nQ. Not less than 75 per cent of the slated amount of \nC!6Hi4F3N5O. m-Av \nA..-..\nRelated substances. Determine by liquid chromatography \n(2.4,14).\nNOTE—Use freshly prepared solutions., ....\nSolvent mixture., 50 volumes of: water and 50 : volumes of \nacetonitrile.. \n. ••\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets: Dissolve a quantity \nof the powder containing 50 mg of Voriconazole in 15 ml of the\nsolvent mixture with the aid of ultrasound for 10 minute$aiu \ndilute to 100.0 ml with the solvent mixture and filter.\nReference solution, A 0.00025 per cent w/v sbluti^-A \nvoriconazole IPRS w the solvent mixture. ,: dT 7\nChromatographic system '' • ■' '•; \n■ n - ■ •:• a■\n- a stainless steel column 15 cm x 4.6 mm, packed\noctydecasilane bonded to porous silica (5;pm).? \n- mobile phase: a mixture, of 70 volumes of\nammonium dihydrogen phosphate, adjusted to pH £ q \nwith ammonia and 30 volumes of acetonitrile.^ \n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n. 7 \"f\n- spectrophotometer set at 255 nm,' ■'1'■'' \na? a\n- injection volume. 20 ul. .... \n. m u . . ¿’•m?.....\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 thebreticalplates and \nthe tailing factor is not more than 2.0. \n. ; : \n, ; ..\nInject the reference solution and the test solution,; In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution, the area of any \nsecondary peak is not more than the area of the principal peak \nin-the chromatogram obtained with-.the;reference solution \n(0.5 per cent) and the sum of the areas of all the secondary \npeaks is not more than twice the; area of the; principal peakin \nthe chromatogram obtained with the reference solution (LO \nper cent). \n■\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets,\nAssay. Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14).\nSolvent mixture. Equal volumes of water and acetonitrile.\nTest solution. Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse a quantity \nof the powder containing 5 0 mg of Voriconazole in 75 ml of the \nsolvent mixture with the aid of ultrasound for 10 minutes and \ndilute to 100.0 ml with the solvent mixture and filter;Dilute 5.0 \nml of the solution to 50.0 ml with the solvent mixture. v;\nReference solution. A 0.005 per cent w/vsolution of\nvoriconazole IPRS in the solvent mixture. \nhuh7 i\nChromatographic system \nm\n- a stainless sted column 15 cm x' 4.6 mm, packed with\noctadecylsilane bonded to porous silica (5 pm), \nmobile phase:, a mixture of 50 volumes of 0.04 M \nammonium, dihydrogen phosphate, adjusted to pH.6.0 \nwith ammonia and 50 volumes of acetonitrile,\n- flow rate: 1 ml per minute, \n:\n- spectrophotometer set at 255 nm,\n- injection volume: 20 pl.\nInject the reference solution. The test is not valid unless the \ncolumn efficiency is not less than 2000 theoretical plates, the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 2.0 per cent.\nInject the reference solution and the.test solution., , \nCalculate the content of C16H;4Ei’NsO in the tablets..-\nStorage. Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°.\n' Híá?; ■■■ ■..■.<■ S';:\n■ v\nk 'WÄr\n■'•;-4plKä^/Z'\n■WW\nC19H15NaO.f \nMol- Wt. 330.3\nWarfarin Sodiuni is sodium2roxo-3-[(l7?*S)-3-oxo-l-phenyl- \nbutyl]-2//-l -benzopyran-4-olate.\nV/arfarinSodium contains not Idss than 98.0 per cent and not \nmore than 102.0, per cent of C^H^NaC^,calculated on the \nanhydrous basis.\nCategory. Anticoagulant\nDescription. A white powder; hygroscopic.\nIdentification ;; y ■ \n¡\nTe^ fÀmay be omitted iftests B, C, D and E are carried out.\nTests B and D may be omitted if tests A, C and E are carried\nA. Dissolve 1 g in 25 ml of water, add 2 ml of 2 M hydrochloric \nacid'-.and filter. Wash the residue with water and dry over \nphosphorus pentoxide. ‘ \n- '■'■'■■■ ■ - ■ z ■ '■\nOn the. residue, determine by infrared absorption \nspectrophotometry (2.4.6). Compare the spectrum with that \nobtained with warfarin sodium treated in the same \nmanner or with the reference spectrum of warfarin.\nB. In the test for Related substances, the principal peak in the \nchromatogramobtained withthe test solution.corrcspondsto \nthe peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n!(c). \na i...,.,. . .\nC¿ Dissolv