tive retention time with reference to xylometazoline\nfor xylometazoline impurity Ais about 0.79."},{"name":"Identification","text":"Inject reference solution (b). The test is not valid unless the \nresolution between the peaks due to xylometazoline and \nxylometazoline impurity A is not less than 2.5.\nInject reference solution (a), (c) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution the area of the \npeak due to xylometazoline impurity A is not more than the \narea of the corresponding peak in the chromatogram obtained \nwith reference solution (c) (0.2 per cent) and the area of any \nother secondary peak is not more than the area of the principal \npeak in thé chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(a)(0.1.per cent). The sum of areas of all the secondary peaks \nIsfrotimore than 5 times the area of the principal peak in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (a) (0.5 per \ncent). Ignore any peak with an area less than 0.5 times the area \nof the principal peak in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (a) (0.05 per cent)."},{"name":"Tests","text":"hrbhj(2.4.14). Moisten the residue obtained in the test for \nSulphated ash with 5 ml of hydrochloric acid, evaporate to \n&yness and dissolve in sufficient water to produce 50 ml.\n10 ml of the resulting solution complies with the limit test for \niron (50 ppm)."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/xylometazoline-hydrochloride","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Xylometazoline Hydrochloride"},"edition":"ip-2010","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Xylometazoline Hydrochloride\nCI6H2~2,HCI\nMol. Wt. 280.8\nXylometazoline Hydrochloride is 2-(4-tert-butyl-\n2,6-dimethylbenzyl)-2-inlidazoline hydrochloride.\nXylometazoline Hydrochloride contains not less than 99.0 per\ncent and not more than 101.0 per cent of C16H24N2' HCl,\ncalculated on the dried basis.\nCategory. Sympathomimetic amine.\nDescription. A white or almost wh