.0 per cent."}]},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/zidovudine-lamivudine-and-nevirapine-tablets","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Zidovudine, Lamivudine and Nevirapine Tablets"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"ZIDOVUDINE, LAMIVUDINE AND NEVIRAPINE TABLETS\n73,-ch.loro-3’.de<>xythymidine, A\ns2,4-dihydroxy-5-methy pyrimidine; thymine,.\n91 -(2-deoxy-f”-D’ribifuranosyl)-5--methyl uracil,\nl0l-(3-azido-2,3-dideoxy-f’-D-threó-pentafuranosyl)-thymidine,\n111 -(3-(3-(3-az!dó-2,3-didéóxy-pentofuranosyl))-5-methyl-2,6-dioxo- \n3,6-dihydropyrimidin<l;ryl)T2;3 -idide.oxypent:ofuranqsyl)-5- \nmethylpyrimidineA,4-dione. \n'--w\nThefretentipnitime.of lamivudine, zidovudine, nevirapine and \nnevirapine impurity Apeaks are about 18,5 minutes; 31 minutes, \n40.6 minutes and 45 minutes respectively.\nInject reference solution (a) and (d). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to lamivudine \ndiastereomer and lamivudine is not less than 1.5 and between \nzidovudine and zidovudine impurity B is not less than 1.5 in \nthe chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a), the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 5.0 per cent, \nfor the peaks due to lamivudine, nevirapine related compound \nA and zidovudine in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (d); '< \nx \n-\nInject reference solution (d) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution; the area of any \npeak corresponding to carboxylic acid impurity, lamivudine \ndistereomer, each of, is not more than 1.66 times the area of the \npeak due tb lamivudine in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (d) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak \ncorresponding to nevirapine impurity A; nevirapine impurity \nB and nevirapine impurity C, each of, is not more, than 1.25 \ntimes the area of peak due to nevirapine impurity A;m the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (d) (0.5 per \ncent), the area of any peak corresponding to zidovudine \nimpurity A (stavudinc), zidovudine impurity B, thymidine; \nzidovudine threo isomers and zidovudine thymidine adduct, \neach of, is not more than .1.25 times the area of the peak due to \nzidovudine in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (d) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding \nto zidovudine impurity (thymine) is not more thari2f5 times \nthe area of the peak due to zidovudine in< the chromatogram \nobtained tyith reference solution (d) (;1 .Q per cent), the area of \nany other secondary peak is not more than1.66 times the area \nof the peak due to lamivudine in the chromatogr am obtained \nwith reference solution (d) (0.5 per cent). The sum of all the\nimpurities is not more than 2.5 per cent. '! '\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay . Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). - ;\nTest solution: Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse' a quantity \nof the powder containing, about 100 mg pf Zidovudine and \ntransfer to a 200-ml volumetric flask. Add about 20 ml of \nmethanol, mix with the aid of ultrasound for\n10 minutes, dilute to volume with water, mix and fdter. Further \ndilute 10.0ml ofthe filtrate to 25.0 mlwith water.: \n;\nReference solution: Weigh 1 OOrng of zidovudine IPRS^ \nof lamivudine IPRSand 65 mg oínevirapine IPRS and tra \nto a 200-ml volumetric flask. Add about 20 ml of methar$[\nwith the aid of ultrasound to dissolve, dilute, to vohiiu^^^\nwqter and mix. Further dilute .10.0 ml ofthe solution to \nwithwaAr. \nA w.,- \n.\nUse the chromatographic system as described \nDissolution.\n........ p.,. \nz \nInject the reference solution. The test is’ hot valid unles^B\ntailing factor for?the. individual peaks due to zidovud^s \nlamivudine and nevirapine is not more than2.0 and the rela^: ' \nstandard deviation for replicate injections of all the itnajyte - \npcaks is not more than 2.0 per cent. ■<’ \n■< ■\nInject the reference solution and the test solution and measun/ \nthe .responses for the majorpeaks. - ;\nCalculate the contents of C10H.3N5O4, CsHj.NjOjS and \nC15Hl4N4O in the tablets. ,\nStorage. Store protected from moisture. ; ; \n. a h"},"sections":[{"name":"CONTENT","text":"ZIDOVUDINE, LAMIVUDINE AND NEVIRAPINE TABLETS\n73,-ch.loro-3’.de<>xythymidine, A\ns2,4-dihydroxy-5-methy pyrimidine; thymine,.\n91 -(2-deoxy-f”-D’ribifuranosyl)-5--methyl uracil,\nl0l-(3-azido-2,3-dideoxy-f’-D-threó-pentafuranosyl)-thymidine,\n111 -(3-(3-(3-az!dó-2,3-didéóxy-pentofuranosyl))-5-methyl-2,6-dioxo- \n3,6-dihydropyrimidin<l;ryl)T2;3 -idide.oxypent:ofuranqsyl)-5- \nmethylpyrimidineA,4-dione. \n'--w\nThefretentipnitime.of lamivudine, zidovudine, nevirapine and \nnevirapine impurity Apeaks are about 18,5 minutes; 31 minutes, \n40.6 minutes and 45 minutes respectively.\nInject reference solution (a) and (d). The test is not valid unless \nthe resolution between the peaks due to lamivudine \ndiastereomer and lamivudine is not less than 1.5 and between \nzidovudine and zidovudine impurity B is not less than 1.5 in \nthe chromatogram obtained with reference solution (a), the \ntailing factor is not more than 2.0 and the relative standard \ndeviation for replicate injections is not more than 5.0 per cent, \nfor the peaks due to lamivudine, nevirapine related compound \nA and zidovudine in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (d); '< \nx \n-\nInject reference solution (d) and the test solution. In the \nchromatogram obtained with the test solution; the area of any \npeak corresponding to carboxylic acid impurity, lamivudine \ndistereomer, each of, is not more than 1.66 times the area of the \npeak due tb lamivudine in the chromatogram obtained with \nreference solution (d) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak \ncorresponding to nevirapine impurity A; nevirapine impurity \nB and nevirapine impurity C, each of, is not more, than 1.25 \ntimes the area of peak due to nevirapine impurity A;m the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (d) (0.5 per \ncent), the area of any peak corresponding to zidovudine \nimpurity A (stavudinc), zidovudine impurity B, thymidine; \nzidovudine threo isomers and zidovudine thymidine adduct, \neach of, is not more than .1.25 times the area of the peak due to \nzidovudine in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (d) (0.5 per cent), the area of any peak corresponding \nto zidovudine impurity (thymine) is not more thari2f5 times \nthe area of the peak due to zidovudine in< the chromatogram \nobtained tyith reference solution (d) (;1 .Q per cent), the area of \nany other secondary peak is not more than1.66 times the area \nof the peak due to lamivudine in the chromatogr am obtained \nwith reference solution (d) (0.5 per cent). The sum of all the\nimpurities is not more than 2.5 per cent. '! '\nOther tests. Comply with the tests stated under Tablets.\nAssay . Determine by liquid chromatography (2.4.14). - ;\nTest solution: Weigh and powder 20 tablets. Disperse' a quantity \nof the powder containing, about 100 mg pf Zidovudine and \ntransfer to a 200-ml volumetric flask. Add about 20 ml of \nmethanol, mix with the aid of ultrasound for\n10 minutes, dilute to volume with water, mix and fdter. Further \ndilute 10.0ml ofthe filtrate to 25.0 mlwith water.: \n;\nReference solution: Weigh 1 OOrng of zidovudine IPRS^ \nof lamivudine IPRSand 65 mg oínevirapine IPRS and tra \nto a 200-ml volumetric flask. Add about 20 ml of methar$[\nwith the aid of ultrasound to dissolve, dilute, to vohiiu^^^\nwqter and mix. Further dilute .10.0 ml ofthe solution to \nwithwaAr. \nA w.,- \n.\nUse the chromatographic system as described \nDissolution.\n........ p.,. \nz \nInject the reference solution. The test is’ hot valid unles^B\ntailing factor for?the. individual peaks due to zidovud^s \nlamivudine and nevirapine is not more than2.0 and the rela^: ' \nstandard deviati